ne location and positional information, and the energy source type and parameters used to acquire the seismic line data."]}],"relatedRecords":[],"capabilityRecords":[]},{"name":"Geophysical Surveys - All","hidden":false,"description":"Descriptions of geophysical datasets, their associated surveys, and the methods used for delivery of those datasets. Includes datasets collected from airborne, land, and marine surveys conducted or managed by Geoscience Australia and its predecessor agencies, as well as data and surveys from State and Territory geological survey agencies.","id":"ga-geophysicalsurveys-all","proxyUrl":null,"proxyGetFeatureInfoUrl":null,"proxyCountUrl":null,"proxyStyleUrl":null,"proxyDownloadUrl":null,"mapStyles":null,"feature_count":0,"singleTile":false,"legendImg":null,"previewImg":null,"group":"Geophysical Survey Datasets (GADDS)","layerMode":"NA","supportsCsvDownloads":true,"cswRecords":[{"name":"Geophysical Survey Datasets","resourceProvider":"Unknown","id":"29447cdcac1b6f8c19dd2e3f147889bdf0a1ab8e","recordInfoUrl":"https://portal.auscope.org.au/geonetwork/srv/eng/catalog.search#/metadata/29447cdcac1b6f8c19dd2e3f147889bdf0a1ab8e","description":"Descriptions of geophysical datasets, their associated surveys, and the methods used for delivery of those datasets.  Includes datasets collected from airborne, land, and marine surveys conducted or managed by Geoscience Australia and its predecessor agencies, as well as data and surveys from State and Territory geological survey agencies","noCache":false,"service":false,"adminArea":null,"contactOrg":"Geoscience Australia","contactPerson":null,"funderOrg":"Unknown","authors":[],"onlineResources":[{"url":"https://services.ga.gov.au/gis/geophysical-surveys/ows?SERVICE=WMS&","type":"WMS","name":"gadds:geophysical_survey_datasets","description":"Geophysical Survey Datasets","version":"1.1.1","applicationProfile":"","protocolRequest":""},{"url":"https://services.ga.gov.au/gis/geophysical-surveys/wfs","type":"WFS","name":"gadds:geophysical_survey_datasets","description":"Geophysical Survey Datasets","version":"","applicationProfile":"","protocolRequest":""}],"geographicElements":[{"type":"bbox","eastBoundLongitude":170.0,"westBoundLongitude":100.0,"northBoundLatitude":-8.0,"southBoundLatitude":-52.0}],"descriptiveKeywords":["elevation","point data","marine survey","Earth Sciences","line data","ground survey","geophysical survey","radiometrics","magnetism","geophysics","electromagnetics","raster data","World","airborne survey","gravity","GADDS"],"datasetURIs":[],"constraints":["","https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0"],"useLimitConstraints":["https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0"],"accessConstraints":[],"childRecords":[],"date":"2023-08-18T00:00:00 UTC","minScale":null,"maxScale":null,"knownLayerIds":["ga-geophysicalsurveys-all"],"knownLayerNames":["Geophysical Surveys - All"],"knownLayerDescriptions":["Descriptions of geophysical datasets, their associated surveys, and the methods used for delivery of those datasets. Includes datasets collected from airborne, land, and marine surveys conducted or managed by Geoscience Australia and its predecessor agencies, as well as data and surveys from State and Territory geological survey agencies."]}],"relatedRecords":[],"capabilityRecords":[]},{"name":"Geophysical Surveys - Gravity","hidden":false,"description":"Gravity data measures small changes in gravity due to changes in the density of rocks beneath the Earth's surface.","id":"ga-geophysicalsurveys-grav","proxyUrl":null,"proxyGetFeatureInfoUrl":null,"proxyCountUrl":null,"proxyStyleUrl":null,"proxyDownloadUrl":null,"mapStyles":null,"feature_count":0,"singleTile":false,"legendImg":null,"previewImg":null,"group":"Geophysical Survey Datasets (GADDS)","layerMode":"NA","supportsCsvDownloads":true,"cswRecords":[{"name":"Geophysical Survey Datasets - Gravity","resourceProvider":"Unknown","id":"e39008033dfde285c9f13f1c44a4474060664f7d","recordInfoUrl":"https://portal.auscope.org.au/geonetwork/srv/eng/catalog.search#/metadata/e39008033dfde285c9f13f1c44a4474060664f7d","description":"Gravity data measures small changes in gravity due to changes in the density of rocks beneath the Earth's surface. The data collected are processed via standard methods with rigorous corrections to ensure the response recorded is that due only to the rocks in the ground. The results produce datasets that can be interpreted to reveal the geological structure of the sub-surface. The processed data is checked for quality by GA geophysicists to ensure that the final data released by GA are fit-for-purpose.","noCache":false,"service":false,"adminArea":null,"contactOrg":"Geoscience Australia","contactPerson":null,"funderOrg":"Unknown","authors":[],"onlineResources":[{"url":"https://services.ga.gov.au/gis/geophysical-surveys/wfs","type":"WFS","name":"gadds:geophysical_datasets_gravity","description":"Geophysical Survey Datasets - Gravity","version":"","applicationProfile":"","protocolRequest":""},{"url":"https://services.ga.gov.au/gis/geophysical-surveys/ows?SERVICE=WMS&","type":"WMS","name":"gadds:geophysical_datasets_gravity","description":"Geophysical Survey Datasets - Gravity","version":"1.1.1","applicationProfile":"","protocolRequest":""}],"geographicElements":[{"type":"bbox","eastBoundLongitude":170.342239379883,"westBoundLongitude":99.6499633789062,"northBoundLatitude":-5.89588403701782,"southBoundLatitude":-52.2176322937012}],"descriptiveKeywords":["marine survey","free air","Earth Sciences","spherical cap","bouguer anomaly","gravity","ground survey","geophysical survey","isostatic residual","World","GADDS"],"datasetURIs":[],"constraints":["","https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0"],"useLimitConstraints":["https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0"],"accessConstraints":[],"childRecords":[],"date":"2023-08-18T00:00:00 UTC","minScale":null,"maxScale":null,"knownLayerIds":["ga-geophysicalsurveys-grav"],"knownLayerNames":["Geophysical Surveys - Gravity"],"knownLayerDescriptions":["Gravity data measures small changes in gravity due to changes in the density of rocks beneath the Earth's surface."]}],"relatedRecords":[],"capabilityRecords":[]},{"name":"Geophysical Surveys - Radiometric","hidden":false,"description":"The radiometric, or gamma-ray spectrometric method, measures the natural variations in the gamma-rays detected near the Earth's surface as the result of the natural radioactive decay of potassium (K), uranium (U) and thorium (Th). Radiometrics can tell us about the distribution of certain soils and rocks.","id":"ga-geophysicalsurveys-radio","proxyUrl":null,"proxyGetFeatureInfoUrl":null,"proxyCountUrl":null,"proxyStyleUrl":null,"proxyDownloadUrl":null,"mapStyles":null,"feature_count":0,"singleTile":false,"legendImg":null,"previewImg":null,"group":"Geophysical Survey Datasets (GADDS)","layerMode":"NA","supportsCsvDownloads":true,"cswRecords":[{"name":"Geophysical Survey Datasets - Radiometric","resourceProvider":"Unknown","id":"4c76b3b96d34ec03ca2eb2efde84849ecd1d71a1","recordInfoUrl":"https://portal.auscope.org.au/geonetwork/srv/eng/catalog.search#/metadata/4c76b3b96d34ec03ca2eb2efde84849ecd1d71a1","description":"The radiometric, or gamma-ray spectrometric method, measures the natural variations in the gamma-rays detected near the Earth's surface as the result of the natural radioactive decay of potassium (K), uranium (U) and thorium (Th). Radiometrics can tell us about the distribution of certain soils and rocks. Geologists and geophysicists routinely use it as a geological mapping tool to tell them where certain rock types change. It is also useful for the study of geomorphology and soils. The data collected are processed via standard methods to ensure the response recorded is that due only to the rocks in the ground. The results produce datasets that can be interpreted to reveal the geological structure of the sub-surface. The processed data is checked for quality by GA geophysicists to ensure that the final data released by GA are fit-for-purpose.","noCache":false,"service":false,"adminArea":null,"contactOrg":"Geoscience Australia","contactPerson":null,"funderOrg":"Unknown","authors":[],"onlineResources":[{"url":"https://services.ga.gov.au/gis/geophysical-surveys/ows?SERVICE=WMS&","type":"WMS","name":"gadds:geophysical_datasets_radiometric","description":"Geophysical Survey Datasets - Radiometric","version":"1.1.1","applicationProfile":"","protocolRequest":""},{"url":"https://services.ga.gov.au/gis/geophysical-surveys/wfs","type":"WFS","name":"gadds:geophysical_datasets_radiometric","description":"Geophysical Survey Datasets - Radiometric","version":"","applicationProfile":"","protocolRequest":""}],"geographicElements":[{"type":"bbox","eastBoundLongitude":154.897003173828,"westBoundLongitude":112.508560180664,"northBoundLatitude":-9.52118301391602,"southBoundLatitude":-44.085319519043}],"descriptiveKeywords":["Earth Sciences","potassium","total count","ratio uranium squared over thorium","line data","geophysical survey","radiometrics","raster data","World","radiometric","dose","ratio thorium over potassium","airborne survey","thorium","uranium","ratio uranium over thorium","ratio uranium over potassium","GADDS"],"datasetURIs":[],"constraints":["","https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0"],"useLimitConstraints":["https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0"],"accessConstraints":[],"childRecords":[],"date":"2023-08-18T00:00:00 UTC","minScale":null,"maxScale":null,"knownLayerIds":["ga-geophysicalsurveys-radio"],"knownLayerNames":["Geophysical Surveys - Radiometric"],"knownLayerDescriptions":["The radiometric, or gamma-ray spectrometric method, measures the natural variations in the gamma-rays detected near the Earth's surface as the result of the natural radioactive decay of potassium (K), uranium (U) and thorium (Th). Radiometrics can tell us about the distribution of certain soils and rocks."]}],"relatedRecords":[],"capabilityRecords":[]},{"name":"Geophysical Surveys - Magnetic","hidden":false,"description":"Total magnetic intensity (TMI) data measures variations in the intensity of the Earth's magnetic field caused by the contrasting content of rock-forming minerals in the Earth crust. Magnetic anomalies can be either positive (field stronger than normal) or negative (field weaker) depending on the susceptibility of the rock.","id":"ga-geophysicalsurveys-mag","proxyUrl":null,"proxyGetFeatureInfoUrl":null,"proxyCountUrl":null,"proxyStyleUrl":null,"proxyDownloadUrl":null,"mapStyles":null,"feature_count":0,"singleTile":false,"legendImg":null,"previewImg":null,"group":"Geophysical Survey Datasets (GADDS)","layerMode":"NA","supportsCsvDownloads":true,"cswRecords":[{"name":"Geophysical Survey Datasets - Magnetic","resourceProvider":"Unknown","id":"c07f45a1004aa751a5280f27d0a6a706607b820d","recordInfoUrl":"https://portal.auscope.org.au/geonetwork/srv/eng/catalog.search#/metadata/c07f45a1004aa751a5280f27d0a6a706607b820d","description":"Total magnetic intensity (TMI) data measures variations in the intensity of the Earth's magnetic field caused by the contrasting content of rock-forming minerals in the Earth crust. Magnetic anomalies can be either positive (field stronger than normal) or negative (field weaker) depending on the susceptibility of the rock. The data are processed via standard methods to ensure the response recorded is that due only to the rocks in the ground. The results produce datasets that can be interpreted to reveal the geological structure of the sub-surface. Once processed and enhanced, magnetic data can be used to locate structural features such as dykes and faults. The processed data is checked for quality by GA geophysicists to ensure that the final data released by GA are fit-for-purpose","noCache":false,"service":false,"adminArea":null,"contactOrg":"Geoscience Australia","contactPerson":null,"funderOrg":"Unknown","authors":[],"onlineResources":[{"url":"https://services.ga.gov.au/gis/geophysical-surveys/wfs","type":"WFS","name":"gadds:geophysical_datasets_magnetic","description":"Geophysical Survey Datasets - Magnetic","version":"","applicationProfile":"","protocolRequest":""},{"url":"https://services.ga.gov.au/gis/geophysical-surveys/ows?SERVICE=WMS&","type":"WMS","name":"gadds:geophysical_datasets_magnetic","description":"Geophysical Survey Datasets - Magnetic","version":"1.1.1","applicationProfile":"","protocolRequest":""}],"geographicElements":[{"type":"bbox","eastBoundLongitude":156.255844116211,"westBoundLongitude":104.746192932129,"northBoundLatitude":-7.9350733757019,"southBoundLatitude":-45.1852416992188}],"descriptiveKeywords":["marine survey","Earth Sciences","line data","magnetism","geophsyical survey","raster data","World","reduced to the pole","airborne survey","total magnetic intensity","variable reduction to the pole","magnetics","GADDS"],"datasetURIs":[],"constraints":["","https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0"],"useLimitConstraints":["https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0"],"accessConstraints":[],"childRecords":[],"date":"2023-08-17T14:00:00 UTC","minScale":null,"maxScale":null,"knownLayerIds":["ga-geophysicalsurveys-mag"],"knownLayerNames":["Geophysical Surveys - Magnetic"],"knownLayerDescriptions":["Total magnetic intensity (TMI) data measures variations in the intensity of the Earth's magnetic field caused by the contrasting content of rock-forming minerals in the Earth crust. Magnetic anomalies can be either positive (field stronger than normal) or negative (field weaker) depending on the susceptibility of the rock."]},{"name":"Geophysical Survey Datasets - Magnetic","resourceProvider":"Unknown","id":"5b542a1f8a1e1f2226876fe733fb5cfabb07f256","recordInfoUrl":"https://portal.auscope.org.au/geonetwork/srv/eng/catalog.search#/metadata/5b542a1f8a1e1f2226876fe733fb5cfabb07f256","description":"Total magnetic intensity (TMI) data measures variations in the intensity of the Earth's magnetic field caused by the contrasting content of rock-forming minerals in the Earth crust. Magnetic anomalies can be either positive (field stronger than normal) or negative (field weaker) depending on the susceptibility of the rock. The data are processed via standard methods to ensure the response recorded is that due only to the rocks in the ground. The results produce datasets that can be interpreted to reveal the geological structure of the sub-surface. Once processed and enhanced, magnetic data can be used to locate structural features such as dykes and faults. The processed data is checked for quality by GA geophysicists to ensure that the final data released by GA are fit-for-purpose","noCache":false,"service":false,"adminArea":null,"contactOrg":"Geoscience Australia","contactPerson":null,"funderOrg":"Unknown","authors":[],"onlineResources":[{"url":"https://services.ga.gov.au/gis/geophysical-surveys/ows?SERVICE=WMS&","type":"WMS","name":"gadds:geophysical_datasets_magnetic","description":"Geophysical Survey Datasets - Magnetic","version":"1.1.1","applicationProfile":"","protocolRequest":""},{"url":"https://services.ga.gov.au/gis/geophysical-surveys/wfs","type":"WFS","name":"gadds:geophysical_datasets_magnetic","description":"Geophysical Survey Datasets - Magnetic","version":"","applicationProfile":"","protocolRequest":""}],"geographicElements":[{"type":"bbox","eastBoundLongitude":156.255844116211,"westBoundLongitude":104.746192932129,"northBoundLatitude":-7.9350733757019,"southBoundLatitude":-45.1852416992188}],"descriptiveKeywords":["marine survey","Earth Sciences","line data","magnetism","geophsyical survey","raster data","World","reduced to the pole","airborne survey","total magnetic intensity","variable reduction to the pole","magnetics","GADDS"],"datasetURIs":[],"constraints":["","https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0"],"useLimitConstraints":["https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0"],"accessConstraints":[],"childRecords":[],"date":"2023-08-18T00:00:00 UTC","minScale":null,"maxScale":null,"knownLayerIds":["ga-geophysicalsurveys-mag"],"knownLayerNames":["Geophysical Surveys - Magnetic"],"knownLayerDescriptions":["Total magnetic intensity (TMI) data measures variations in the intensity of the Earth's magnetic field caused by the contrasting content of rock-forming minerals in the Earth crust. Magnetic anomalies can be either positive (field stronger than normal) or negative (field weaker) depending on the susceptibility of the rock."]}],"relatedRecords":[],"capabilityRecords":[]},{"name":"Geophysical Surveys - Elevation","hidden":false,"description":"Digital Elevation data record the terrain height variations from the processed point-located data recorded during a geophysical survey.","id":"ga-geophysicalsurveys-elev","proxyUrl":null,"proxyGetFeatureInfoUrl":null,"proxyCountUrl":null,"proxyStyleUrl":null,"proxyDownloadUrl":null,"mapStyles":null,"feature_count":0,"singleTile":false,"legendImg":null,"previewImg":null,"group":"Geophysical Survey Datasets (GADDS)","layerMode":"NA","supportsCsvDownloads":true,"cswRecords":[{"name":"Geophysical Survey Datasets - Elevation","resourceProvider":"Unknown","id":"ae52f911a3b8a2ea18f958848afb103a8cd068fa","recordInfoUrl":"https://portal.auscope.org.au/geonetwork/srv/eng/catalog.search#/metadata/ae52f911a3b8a2ea18f958848afb103a8cd068fa","description":"Digital Elevation data record the terrain height variations from the processed point-located data recorded during a geophysical survey. The data acquired are a mass of ground heights representing a terrain surface. The data are either geoidal (representing the vertical distance from a location on the Earth's surface to the geoid) or ellipsoidal (representing the vertical distance from a location on the Earth's surface to the ellipsoid). The data are given in units of meters. The processed data is checked for quality by GA geophysicists to ensure that the final data released by GA are fit-for-purpose.","noCache":false,"service":false,"adminArea":null,"contactOrg":"Geoscience Australia","contactPerson":null,"funderOrg":"Unknown","authors":[],"onlineResources":[{"url":"https://services.ga.gov.au/gis/geophysical-surveys/ows?SERVICE=WMS&","type":"WMS","name":"gadds:geophysical_datasets_elevation","description":"Geophysical Survey Datasets - Elevation","version":"1.1.1","applicationProfile":"","protocolRequest":""},{"url":"https://services.ga.gov.au/gis/geophysical-surveys/wfs","type":"WFS","name":"gadds:geophysical_datasets_elevation","description":"Geophysical Survey Datasets - Elevation","version":"","applicationProfile":"","protocolRequest":""}],"geographicElements":[{"type":"bbox","eastBoundLongitude":153.890777587891,"westBoundLongitude":112.51286315918,"northBoundLatitude":-10.4854135513306,"southBoundLatitude":-44.0803108215332}],"descriptiveKeywords":["elevation","Earth Sciences","airborne survey","digital elevation model","line data","geophysical survey","geoid height","ellipsoid height","raster data","World","GADDS"],"datasetURIs":[],"constraints":["","https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0"],"useLimitConstraints":["https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0"],"accessConstraints":[],"childRecords":[],"date":"2023-08-18T00:00:00 UTC","minScale":null,"maxScale":null,"knownLayerIds":["ga-geophysicalsurveys-elev"],"knownLayerNames":["Geophysical Surveys - Elevation"],"knownLayerDescriptions":["Digital Elevation data record the terrain height variations from the processed point-located data recorded during a geophysical survey."]}],"relatedRecords":[],"capabilityRecords":[]},{"name":"Bouguer Gravity Anomaly 2016","hidden":false,"description":"This gravity anomaly grid is derived from observations stored in the Australian National Gravity Database ANGD) as at February 2016 as well as data from the 2013 New South Wales Riverina gravity survey.","id":"ga-geophys-1","proxyUrl":null,"proxyGetFeatureInfoUrl":null,"proxyCountUrl":null,"proxyStyleUrl":null,"proxyDownloadUrl":null,"mapStyles":null,"feature_count":0,"singleTile":false,"legendImg":null,"previewImg":null,"group":"Geophysics - National Geophysical Compilation","layerMode":"NA","cswRecords":[{"name":"Bouguer Gravity Anomaly Grid of Onshore Australia 2016","resourceProvider":"Unknown","id":"f0886_1142_1614_4044","recordInfoUrl":"https://geonetwork.nci.org.au/geonetwork/srv/eng/catalog.search#/metadata/f0886_1142_1614_4044","description":"This gravity anomaly grid is derived from observations stored in the Australian National Gravity Database (ANGD) as at February 2016 as well as data from the 2013 New South Wales Riverina gravity survey. Out of the almost 1.8 million records in the ANGD approximately 1.4 million stations together with 19,558 stations from the Riverina survey were used to generate this grid. This product shows spherical cap Bouguer anomalies over onshore continental Australia. The data used in this grid has been acquired by the Commonwealth, State and Territory Governments, the mining and exploration industry, universities and research organisations from the 1940's to the present day. The spherical cap Bouguer anomalies in this grid are the combination of Bullard A and B corrections to the Free Air anomaly values using a density of 2670 kg/m^3.\n\n\n--\nThis record represents data published by NCI. It uses catalogue metadata modified from Geoscience Australia. See our Record Lineage Information for more details.","noCache":false,"service":false,"adminArea":null,"contactOrg":"Commonwealth of Australia (Geoscience Australia)","contactPerson":null,"funderOrg":"Unknown","authors":["Nakamura, A.","Nakamura, A.","Nakamura, A.","Nakamura, A.","Nakamura, A."],"onlineResources":[{"url":"https://gsky.nci.org.au/ows/national_geophysical_compilations?service=WMS&version=1.1.1&request=GetCapabilities","type":"WMS","name":"gravmap2016_grid_grv_scba","description":"NCI GSKY Web Map Service (WMS)","version":"1.1.1","applicationProfile":"","protocolRequest":""},{"url":"https://gsky.nci.org.au/ows/national_geophysical_compilations?service=WCS&version=1.0.0&request=GetCapabilities","type":"WCS","name":"gravmap2016_grid_grv_scba","description":"NCI GSKY Web Coverage Service (WCS)","version":"","applicationProfile":"","protocolRequest":""},{"url":"https://thredds.nci.org.au/thredds/fileServer/iv65/Geoscience_Australia_Geophysics_Reference_Data_Collection/national_geophysical_compilations/Gravmap2016/Gravmap2016-grid-grv_scba.nc","type":"WWW","name":"Gravmap2016-grid-grv_scba","description":"NCI NetCDF file download via HTTP","version":"","applicationProfile":"","protocolRequest":""},{"url":"https://doi.org/10.4225/25/579AB36FB071A","type":"WWW","name":"Geoscience Australia Source Record","description":"","version":"","applicationProfile":"","protocolRequest":""}],"geographicElements":[{"type":"bbox","eastBoundLongitude":153.707994,"westBoundLongitude":112.859628,"northBoundLatitude":-8.979204,"southBoundLatitude":-43.777812}],"descriptiveKeywords":["gravity",""],"datasetURIs":["10.25914/5f756827e3eb2"],"constraints":["https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","Licences for datasets within this collection may vary. Check individual files for the relevant licence that applies.","RestrictionCode: license","Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International License"],"useLimitConstraints":["Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International License","RestrictionCode: license"],"accessConstraints":["RestrictionCode: license"],"childRecords":[],"date":"2018-04-20T00:00:00 UTC","minScale":null,"maxScale":null,"knownLayerIds":["ga-geophys-1"],"knownLayerNames":["Bouguer Gravity Anomaly 2016"],"knownLayerDescriptions":["This gravity anomaly grid is derived from observations stored in the Australian National Gravity Database ANGD) as at February 2016 as well as data from the 2013 New South Wales Riverina gravity survey."]}],"relatedRecords":[],"capabilityRecords":[]},{"name":"Complete Bouguer Gravity Anomaly 2016","hidden":false,"description":"This gravity anomaly grid is derived from observations stored in the Australian National Gravity Database ANGD) as at February 2016 as well as data from the 2013 New South Wales Riverina gravity survey.","id":"ga-geophys-2","proxyUrl":null,"proxyGetFeatureInfoUrl":null,"proxyCountUrl":null,"proxyStyleUrl":null,"proxyDownloadUrl":null,"mapStyles":null,"feature_count":0,"singleTile":false,"legendImg":null,"previewImg":null,"group":"Geophysics - National Geophysical Compilation","layerMode":"NA","cswRecords":[{"name":"Complete Bouguer Gravity Anomaly Grid of Onshore Australia 2016","resourceProvider":"Commonwealth of Australia (Geoscience Australia)","id":"f2848_9429_6275_5590","recordInfoUrl":"https://geonetwork.nci.org.au/geonetwork/srv/eng/catalog.search#/metadata/f2848_9429_6275_5590","description":"This gravity anomaly grid is derived from observations stored in the Australian National Gravity Database (ANGD) as at February 2016 as well as data from the 2013 New South Wales Riverina gravity survey. Out of the approximately 1.8 million gravity observations 1,371,998 gravity stations in the ANGD together with 19,558 stations from the Riverina survey were used to generate this grid. The grid shows complete Bouguer anomalies over onshore continental Australia. The data used in this grid has been acquired by the Commonwealth, State and Territory Governments, the mining and exploration industry, universities and research organisations from the 1940's to the present day. \r\nTerrain corrections to gravity were calculated using both offshore bathymetry and onshore topography data. These terrain corrections were applied to the spherical cap Bouguer anomalies used in the Bouguer Gravity Anomaly Grid of Onshore Australia 2016 to produce the complete Bouguer anomaly values shown in this grid.\n\n\n--\nThis record represents data published by NCI. It uses catalogue metadata modified from Geoscience Australia. See our Record Lineage Information for more details.","noCache":false,"service":false,"adminArea":null,"contactOrg":"Commonwealth of Australia (Geoscience Australia)","contactPerson":null,"funderOrg":"Unknown","authors":["Nakamura, A.","Nakamura, A.","Nakamura, A.","Nakamura, A."],"onlineResources":[{"url":"https://gsky.nci.org.au/ows/national_geophysical_compilations?service=WMS&version=1.1.1&request=GetCapabilities","type":"WMS","name":"gravmap2016_grid_grv_cscba","description":"NCI GSKY Web Map Service (WMS)","version":"1.1.1","applicationProfile":"","protocolRequest":""},{"url":"https://gsky.nci.org.au/ows/national_geophysical_compilations?service=WCS&version=1.0.0&request=GetCapabilities","type":"WCS","name":"gravmap2016_grid_grv_cscba","description":"NCI GSKY Web Coverage Service (WCS)","version":"","applicationProfile":"","protocolRequest":""},{"url":"https://thredds.nci.org.au/thredds/fileServer/iv65/Geoscience_Australia_Geophysics_Reference_Data_Collection/national_geophysical_compilations/Gravmap2016/Gravmap2016-grid-grv_cscba.nc","type":"WWW","name":"Gravmap2016-grid-grv_cscba","description":"NCI NetCDF file download via HTTP","version":"","applicationProfile":"","protocolRequest":""},{"url":"https://doi.org/10.4225/25/579AB5FC3CAD7","type":"WWW","name":"Geoscience Australia Source Record","description":"","version":"","applicationProfile":"","protocolRequest":""}],"geographicElements":[{"type":"bbox","eastBoundLongitude":153.707994,"westBoundLongitude":112.859628,"northBoundLatitude":-8.979204,"southBoundLatitude":-43.777812}],"descriptiveKeywords":["gravity",""],"datasetURIs":["10.25914/5f7567c199dc8"],"constraints":["https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","Licences for datasets within this collection may vary. Check individual files for the relevant licence that applies.","RestrictionCode: license","Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International License"],"useLimitConstraints":["Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International License","RestrictionCode: license"],"accessConstraints":["RestrictionCode: license"],"childRecords":[],"date":"2018-04-20T00:00:00 UTC","minScale":null,"maxScale":null,"knownLayerIds":["ga-geophys-2"],"knownLayerNames":["Complete Bouguer Gravity Anomaly 2016"],"knownLayerDescriptions":["This gravity anomaly grid is derived from observations stored in the Australian National Gravity Database ANGD) as at February 2016 as well as data from the 2013 New South Wales Riverina gravity survey."]}],"relatedRecords":[],"capabilityRecords":[]},{"name":"Isostatic Residual Gravity Anomaly 2016","hidden":false,"description":"This grid is derived from gravity observations stored in the Australian National Gravity Database ANGD) as at February 2016 as well as data from the 2013 New South Wales Riverina gravity survey.","id":"ga-geophys-3","proxyUrl":null,"proxyGetFeatureInfoUrl":null,"proxyCountUrl":null,"proxyStyleUrl":null,"proxyDownloadUrl":null,"mapStyles":null,"feature_count":0,"singleTile":false,"legendImg":null,"previewImg":null,"group":"Geophysics - National Geophysical Compilation","layerMode":"NA","cswRecords":[{"name":"Isostatic Residual Gravity Anomaly Grid of Onshore Australia 2016","resourceProvider":"Unknown","id":"f4523_7439_0612_0991","recordInfoUrl":"https://geonetwork.nci.org.au/geonetwork/srv/eng/catalog.search#/metadata/f4523_7439_0612_0991","description":"This grid is derived from gravity observations stored in the Australian National Gravity Database (ANGD) as at February 2016 as well as data from the 2013 New South Wales Riverina gravity survey. Out of the approximately 1.8 million gravity observations 1,371,998 gravity stations in the ANGD together with 19,558 stations from the Riverina survey were used to generate this image. The grid shows isostatic residual gravity anomalies over onshore continental Australia. The data used in this grid has been acquired by the Commonwealth, State and Territory Governments, the mining and exploration industry, universities and research organisations from the 1940's to the present day. \r\nThe isostatic corrections were based on the assumption that topographic loads are compensated at depth by crustal roots following the Airy-Heiskanen isostatic principle. A crustal density of 2670 kg/m3 was used for the isostatic correction, with an assumed density contrast between the crust and mantle of 400 kg/m3. An initial average depth to Moho at sea level of 37 km was used in the calculation. The isostatic corrections were then applied to the Complete Bouguer Gravity Anomaly Grid of Onshore Australia 2016 to produce the Isostatic Residual Gravity Anomaly Grid of Onshore Australia 2016.\n\n\n--\nThis record represents data published by NCI. It uses catalogue metadata modified from Geoscience Australia. See our Record Lineage Information for more details.","noCache":false,"service":false,"adminArea":null,"contactOrg":"Commonwealth of Australia (Geoscience Australia)","contactPerson":null,"funderOrg":"Unknown","authors":["Nakamura, A.","Nakamura, A.","Nakamura, A.","Nakamura, A.","Nakamura, A."],"onlineResources":[{"url":"https://gsky.nci.org.au/ows/national_geophysical_compilations?service=WMS&version=1.1.1&request=GetCapabilities","type":"WMS","name":"gravmap2016_grid_grv_ir","description":"NCI GSKY Web Map Service (WMS)","version":"1.1.1","applicationProfile":"","protocolRequest":""},{"url":"https://gsky.nci.org.au/ows/national_geophysical_compilations?service=WCS&version=1.0.0&request=GetCapabilities","type":"WCS","name":"gravmap2016_grid_grv_ir","description":"NCI GSKY Web Coverage Service (WCS)","version":"","applicationProfile":"","protocolRequest":""},{"url":"https://thredds.nci.org.au/thredds/fileServer/iv65/Geoscience_Australia_Geophysics_Reference_Data_Collection/national_geophysical_compilations/Gravmap2016/Gravmap2016-grid-grv_ir.nc","type":"WWW","name":"Gravmap2016-grid-grv_ir","description":"NCI NetCDF file download via HTTP","version":"","applicationProfile":"","protocolRequest":""},{"url":"https://doi.org/10.4225/25/57A0243A36A9F","type":"WWW","name":"Geoscience Australia Source Record","description":"","version":"","applicationProfile":"","protocolRequest":""}],"geographicElements":[{"type":"bbox","eastBoundLongitude":154.169312,"westBoundLongitude":112.504312,"northBoundLatitude":-10.102527,"southBoundLatitude":-44.267827}],"descriptiveKeywords":["gravity",""],"datasetURIs":["10.25914/5f7567f94a5cd"],"constraints":["https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","Licences for datasets within this collection may vary. Check individual files for the relevant licence that applies.","RestrictionCode: license","Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International License"],"useLimitConstraints":["Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International License","RestrictionCode: license"],"accessConstraints":["RestrictionCode: license"],"childRecords":[],"date":"2018-04-20T00:00:00 UTC","minScale":null,"maxScale":null,"knownLayerIds":["ga-geophys-3"],"knownLayerNames":["Isostatic Residual Gravity Anomaly 2016"],"knownLayerDescriptions":["This grid is derived from gravity observations stored in the Australian National Gravity Database ANGD) as at February 2016 as well as data from the 2013 New South Wales Riverina gravity survey."]}],"relatedRecords":[],"capabilityRecords":[]},{"name":"Radmap v4 2019 filtered pct K","hidden":false,"description":"Radiometric Grid of Australia (Radmap). The filtered potassium grid is a derivative of the 2019 radiometric or gamma-ray grid of Australia.","id":"ga-geophys-4","proxyUrl":null,"proxyGetFeatureInfoUrl":null,"proxyCountUrl":null,"proxyStyleUrl":null,"proxyDownloadUrl":null,"mapStyles":null,"feature_count":0,"singleTile":false,"legendImg":null,"previewImg":null,"group":"Geophysics - National Geophysical Compilation","layerMode":"NA","cswRecords":[{"name":"Radiometric Grid of Australia (Radmap) v4 2019 filtered pct potassium grid","resourceProvider":"Resources Division","id":"f4273_6870_1273_8584","recordInfoUrl":"https://geonetwork.nci.org.au/geonetwork/srv/eng/catalog.search#/metadata/f4273_6870_1273_8584","description":"The filtered potassium grid is a derivative of the 2019 radiometric or gamma-ray grid of Australia. The radiometric, or gamma-ray spectrometric method, measures the natural variations in the gamma-rays detected near the Earth's surface as the result of the natural radioactive decay of potassium, uranium and thorium.  The data are collected on airborne geophysical surveys conducted by Commonwealth, State and Northern Territory Governments and the private sector.\r\nThe 2019 filtered potassium grid has a cell size of about 100m (0.001 degrees) and shows potassium element concentrations of the Australia region. It was obtained by applying a low-pass filter to the original potassium grid. Potassium is the seventh most abundant element in the Earth's crust. This potassium concentration grid can be used to locate minerals and compounds containing potassium.\n\n\n--\nThis record represents data published by NCI. It uses catalogue metadata modified from Geoscience Australia. See our Record Lineage Information for more details.","noCache":false,"service":false,"adminArea":null,"contactOrg":"Commonwealth of Australia (Geoscience Australia)","contactPerson":null,"funderOrg":"Unknown","authors":["Poudjom Djomani, Y.","Minty, B.R.S.","Poudjom Djomani, Y.","Minty, B.R.S.","Poudjom Djomani, Y.","Minty, B.R.S.","Poudjom Djomani, Y.","Poudjom Djomani, Y.","Minty, B.R.S."],"onlineResources":[{"url":"https://gsky.nci.org.au/ows/national_geophysical_compilations?service=WMS&version=1.1.1&request=GetCapabilities","type":"WMS","name":"radmap2019_grid_k_conc_filtered_awags_rad_2019","description":"NCI GSKY Web Map Service (WMS)","version":"1.1.1","applicationProfile":"","protocolRequest":""},{"url":"https://gsky.nci.org.au/ows/national_geophysical_compilations?service=WCS&version=1.0.0&request=GetCapabilities","type":"WCS","name":"radmap2019_grid_k_conc_filtered_awags_rad_2019","description":"NCI GSKY Web Coverage Service (WCS)","version":"","applicationProfile":"","protocolRequest":""},{"url":"https://thredds.nci.org.au/thredds/fileServer/iv65/Geoscience_Australia_Geophysics_Reference_Data_Collection/national_geophysical_compilations/Radmap2019/Radmap2019-grid-k_conc-Filtered-AWAGS_RAD_2019.nc","type":"WWW","name":"Radmap2019-grid-k_conc-Filtered-AWAGS_RAD_2019","description":"NCI NetCDF file download via HTTP","version":"","applicationProfile":"","protocolRequest":""},{"url":"https://doi.org/10.26186/5dd48d628f4f6","type":"WWW","name":"Geoscience Australia Source Record","description":"","version":"","applicationProfile":"","protocolRequest":""}],"geographicElements":[{"type":"bbox","eastBoundLongitude":153.6715,"westBoundLongitude":112.7175,"northBoundLatitude":-9.0005,"southBoundLatitude":-43.7615}],"descriptiveKeywords":["airborne digital data",""],"datasetURIs":["10.25914/5f7565a94c9ec"],"constraints":["https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","Licences for datasets within this collection may vary. Check individual files for the relevant licence that applies.","RestrictionCode: license","Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International License"],"useLimitConstraints":["Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International License","RestrictionCode: license"],"accessConstraints":["RestrictionCode: license"],"childRecords":[],"date":"2018-04-20T00:00:00 UTC","minScale":null,"maxScale":null,"knownLayerIds":["ga-geophys-4"],"knownLayerNames":["Radmap v4 2019 filtered pct K"],"knownLayerDescriptions":["Radiometric Grid of Australia (Radmap). The filtered potassium grid is a derivative of the 2019 radiometric or gamma-ray grid of Australia."]}],"relatedRecords":[],"capabilityRecords":[]},{"name":"Radmap v4 2019 filtered ppm Th","hidden":false,"description":"Radiometric Grid of Australia (Radmap). The filtered thorium grid is a derivative of the 2019 radiometric or gamma-ray grid of Australia.","id":"ga-geophys-5","proxyUrl":null,"proxyGetFeatureInfoUrl":null,"proxyCountUrl":null,"proxyStyleUrl":null,"proxyDownloadUrl":null,"mapStyles":null,"feature_count":0,"singleTile":false,"legendImg":null,"previewImg":null,"group":"Geophysics - National Geophysical Compilation","layerMode":"NA","cswRecords":[{"name":"Radiometric Grid of Australia (Radmap) v4 2019 filtered ppm thorium","resourceProvider":"Resources Division","id":"f1561_4208_1403_5295","recordInfoUrl":"https://geonetwork.nci.org.au/geonetwork/srv/eng/catalog.search#/metadata/f1561_4208_1403_5295","description":"The filtered thorium grid is a derivative of the 2019 radiometric or gamma-ray grid of Australia. The radiometric, or gamma-ray spectrometric method, measures the natural variations in the gamma-rays detected near the Earth's surface as the result of the natural radioactive decay of potassium (K), uranium (U) and thorium (Th).  The data are collected on airborne geophysical surveys conducted by Commonwealth, State and Northern Territory Governments and the private sector. \r\nThe 2019 filtered thorium grid was derived by seamlessly merging over 600 airborne gamma-ray spectrometric surveys. The final grid has a cell size of about 100m (0.001 degrees) and shows thorium element concentrations of the Australia region.\n\n\n--\nThis record represents data published by NCI. It uses catalogue metadata modified from Geoscience Australia. See our Record Lineage Information for more details.","noCache":false,"service":false,"adminArea":null,"contactOrg":"Commonwealth of Australia (Geoscience Australia)","contactPerson":null,"funderOrg":"Unknown","authors":["Poudjom Djomani, Y.","Minty, B.R.S.","Poudjom Djomani, Y.","Minty, B.R.S.","Poudjom Djomani, Y.","Minty, B.R.S.","Poudjom Djomani, Y.","Minty, B.R.S.","Poudjom Djomani, Y.","Minty, B.R.S."],"onlineResources":[{"url":"https://gsky.nci.org.au/ows/national_geophysical_compilations?service=WMS&version=1.1.1&request=GetCapabilities","type":"WMS","name":"radmap2019_grid_th_conc_filtered_awags_rad_2019","description":"NCI GSKY Web Map Service (WMS)","version":"1.1.1","applicationProfile":"","protocolRequest":""},{"url":"https://gsky.nci.org.au/ows/national_geophysical_compilations?service=WCS&version=1.0.0&request=GetCapabilities","type":"WCS","name":"radmap2019_grid_th_conc_filtered_awags_rad_2019","description":"NCI GSKY Web Coverage Service (WCS)","version":"","applicationProfile":"","protocolRequest":""},{"url":"https://thredds.nci.org.au/thredds/fileServer/iv65/Geoscience_Australia_Geophysics_Reference_Data_Collection/national_geophysical_compilations/Radmap2019/Radmap2019-grid-th_conc-Filtered-AWAGS_RAD_2019.nc","type":"WWW","name":"Radmap2019-grid-th_conc-Filtered-AWAGS_RAD_2019","description":"NCI NetCDF file download via HTTP","version":"","applicationProfile":"","protocolRequest":""},{"url":"https://doi.org/10.26186/5dd48e3eb6367","type":"WWW","name":"Geoscience Australia Source Record","description":"","version":"","applicationProfile":"","protocolRequest":""}],"geographicElements":[{"type":"bbox","eastBoundLongitude":153.6715,"westBoundLongitude":112.7175,"northBoundLatitude":-9.0005,"southBoundLatitude":-43.7615}],"descriptiveKeywords":["airborne digital data",""],"datasetURIs":["10.25914/5f75659054697"],"constraints":["https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","Licences for datasets within this collection may vary. Check individual files for the relevant licence that applies.","RestrictionCode: license","Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International License"],"useLimitConstraints":["Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International License","RestrictionCode: license"],"accessConstraints":["RestrictionCode: license"],"childRecords":[],"date":"2018-04-20T00:00:00 UTC","minScale":null,"maxScale":null,"knownLayerIds":["ga-geophys-5"],"knownLayerNames":["Radmap v4 2019 filtered ppm Th"],"knownLayerDescriptions":["Radiometric Grid of Australia (Radmap). The filtered thorium grid is a derivative of the 2019 radiometric or gamma-ray grid of Australia."]}],"relatedRecords":[],"capabilityRecords":[]},{"name":"Radmap v4 2019 filtered ppm U","hidden":false,"description":"Radiometric Grid of Australia (Radmap). The filtered uranium grid is a derivative of the 2019 radiometric or gamma-ray grid of Australia.","id":"ga-geophys-6","proxyUrl":null,"proxyGetFeatureInfoUrl":null,"proxyCountUrl":null,"proxyStyleUrl":null,"proxyDownloadUrl":null,"mapStyles":null,"feature_count":0,"singleTile":false,"legendImg":null,"previewImg":null,"group":"Geophysics - National Geophysical Compilation","layerMode":"NA","cswRecords":[{"name":"Radiometric Grid of Australia (Radmap) v4 2019 filtered ppm uranium","resourceProvider":"Resources Division","id":"f6888_9004_5632_3885","recordInfoUrl":"https://geonetwork.nci.org.au/geonetwork/srv/eng/catalog.search#/metadata/f6888_9004_5632_3885","description":"The filtered uranium grid is a derivative of the 2019 radiometric or gamma-ray grid of Australia. The radiometric, or gamma-ray spectrometric method, measures the natural variations in the gamma-rays detected near the Earth's surface as the result of the natural radioactive decay of potassium (K), uranium (U) and thorium (Th).  The data are collected on airborne geophysical surveys conducted by Commonwealth, State and Northern Territory Governments and the private sector.\r\nThe 2019 filtered uranium grid was derived by seamlessly merging over 600 airborne gamma-ray spectrometric surveys. The final grid has a cell size of about 100m (0.001 degrees) and shows uranium element concentrations of the Australia region.\n\n\n--\nThis record represents data published by NCI. It uses catalogue metadata modified from Geoscience Australia. See our Record Lineage Information for more details.","noCache":false,"service":false,"adminArea":null,"contactOrg":"Commonwealth of Australia (Geoscience Australia)","contactPerson":null,"funderOrg":"Unknown","authors":["Poudjom Djomani, Y.","Minty, B.R.S.","Poudjom Djomani, Y.","Minty, B.R.S.","Poudjom Djomani, Y.","Minty, B.R.S.","Poudjom Djomani, Y.","Poudjom Djomani, Y.","Minty, B.R.S."],"onlineResources":[{"url":"https://gsky.nci.org.au/ows/national_geophysical_compilations?service=WMS&version=1.1.1&request=GetCapabilities","type":"WMS","name":"radmap2019_grid_u_conc_filtered_awags_rad_2019","description":"NCI GSKY Web Map Service (WMS)","version":"1.1.1","applicationProfile":"","protocolRequest":""},{"url":"https://gsky.nci.org.au/ows/national_geophysical_compilations?service=WCS&version=1.0.0&request=GetCapabilities","type":"WCS","name":"radmap2019_grid_u_conc_filtered_awags_rad_2019","description":"NCI GSKY Web Coverage Service (WCS)","version":"","applicationProfile":"","protocolRequest":""},{"url":"https://thredds.nci.org.au/thredds/fileServer/iv65/Geoscience_Australia_Geophysics_Reference_Data_Collection/national_geophysical_compilations/Radmap2019/Radmap2019-grid-u_conc-Filtered-AWAGS_RAD_2019.nc","type":"WWW","name":"Radmap2019-grid-u_conc-Filtered-AWAGS_RAD_2019","description":"NCI NetCDF file download via HTTP","version":"","applicationProfile":"","protocolRequest":""},{"url":"https://doi.org/10.26186/5dd48ee78c980","type":"WWW","name":"Geoscience Australia Source Record","description":"","version":"","applicationProfile":"","protocolRequest":""}],"geographicElements":[{"type":"bbox","eastBoundLongitude":153.6715,"westBoundLongitude":112.7175,"northBoundLatitude":-9.0005,"southBoundLatitude":-43.7615}],"descriptiveKeywords":["airborne digital data",""],"datasetURIs":["10.25914/5f7566578b894"],"constraints":["https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","Licences for datasets within this collection may vary. Check individual files for the relevant licence that applies.","RestrictionCode: license","Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International License"],"useLimitConstraints":["Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International License","RestrictionCode: license"],"accessConstraints":["RestrictionCode: license"],"childRecords":[],"date":"2018-04-20T00:00:00 UTC","minScale":null,"maxScale":null,"knownLayerIds":["ga-geophys-6"],"knownLayerNames":["Radmap v4 2019 filtered ppm U"],"knownLayerDescriptions":["Radiometric Grid of Australia (Radmap). The filtered uranium grid is a derivative of the 2019 radiometric or gamma-ray grid of Australia."]}],"relatedRecords":[],"capabilityRecords":[]},{"name":"Radmap v4 2019 filtered terrestrial dose","hidden":false,"description":"Radiometric Grid of Australia (Radmap). The filtered terrestrial dose rate grid is a derivative of the 2019 radiometric or gamma-ray grid of Australia, made of a combination of over 600 individual survey grids.","id":"ga-geophys-7","proxyUrl":null,"proxyGetFeatureInfoUrl":null,"proxyCountUrl":null,"proxyStyleUrl":null,"proxyDownloadUrl":null,"mapStyles":null,"feature_count":0,"singleTile":false,"legendImg":null,"previewImg":null,"group":"Geophysics - National Geophysical Compilation","layerMode":"NA","cswRecords":[{"name":"Radiometric Grid of Australia (Radmap) v4 2019 filtered terrestrial dose rate","resourceProvider":"Resources Division","id":"f5953_4510_9151_5863","recordInfoUrl":"https://geonetwork.nci.org.au/geonetwork/srv/eng/catalog.search#/metadata/f5953_4510_9151_5863","description":"The filtered terrestrial dose rate grid is a derivative of the 2019 radiometric or gamma-ray grid of Australia, made of a combination of over 600 individual survey grids. The radiometric, or gamma-ray spectrometric method, measures the natural variations in the gamma-rays detected near the Earth's surface as the result of the natural radioactive decay of potassium (K), uranium (U) and thorium (Th).  The data are collected on airborne geophysical surveys conducted by Commonwealth, State and Northern Territory Governments and the private sector.\r\nThe terrestrial dose rate grid is derived as a linear combination of the filtered K, U and Th grids. A low pass filter is applied to the unfiltered grid to generate the filtered terrestrial dose rate grid. The grid cell size is about 100m (0.001 degrees).\n\n\n--\nThis record represents data published by NCI. It uses catalogue metadata modified from Geoscience Australia. See our Record Lineage Information for more details.","noCache":false,"service":false,"adminArea":null,"contactOrg":"Commonwealth of Australia (Geoscience Australia)","contactPerson":null,"funderOrg":"Unknown","authors":["Poudjom Djomani, Y.","Minty, B.R.S.","Poudjom Djomani, Y.","Minty, B.R.S.","Poudjom Djomani, Y.","Minty, B.R.S.","Poudjom Djomani, Y.","Minty, B.R.S.","Poudjom Djomani, Y.","Minty, B.R.S."],"onlineResources":[{"url":"https://gsky.nci.org.au/ows/national_geophysical_compilations?service=WMS&version=1.1.1&request=GetCapabilities","type":"WMS","name":"radmap2019_grid_dose_terr_filtered_awags_rad_2019","description":"NCI GSKY Web Map Service (WMS)","version":"1.1.1","applicationProfile":"","protocolRequest":""},{"url":"https://gsky.nci.org.au/ows/national_geophysical_compilations?service=WCS&version=1.0.0&request=GetCapabilities","type":"WCS","name":"radmap2019_grid_dose_terr_filtered_awags_rad_2019","description":"NCI GSKY Web Coverage Service (WCS)","version":"","applicationProfile":"","protocolRequest":""},{"url":"https://thredds.nci.org.au/thredds/fileServer/iv65/Geoscience_Australia_Geophysics_Reference_Data_Collection/national_geophysical_compilations/Radmap2019/Radmap2019-grid-dose_terr-Filtered-AWAGS_RAD_2019.nc","type":"WWW","name":"Radmap2019-grid-dose_terr-Filtered-AWAGS_RAD_2019","description":"NCI NetCDF file download via HTTP","version":"","applicationProfile":"","protocolRequest":""},{"url":"https://doi.org/10.26186/5dd48c423f927","type":"WWW","name":"Geoscience Australia Source Record","description":"","version":"","applicationProfile":"","protocolRequest":""}],"geographicElements":[{"type":"bbox","eastBoundLongitude":153.6715,"westBoundLongitude":112.7175,"northBoundLatitude":-9.0005,"southBoundLatitude":-43.7615}],"descriptiveKeywords":["airborne digital data",""],"datasetURIs":["10.25914/5f75654e8d12a"],"constraints":["https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","Licences for datasets within this collection may vary. Check individual files for the relevant licence that applies.","RestrictionCode: license","Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International License"],"useLimitConstraints":["Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International License","RestrictionCode: license"],"accessConstraints":["RestrictionCode: license"],"childRecords":[],"date":"2018-04-20T00:00:00 UTC","minScale":null,"maxScale":null,"knownLayerIds":["ga-geophys-7"],"knownLayerNames":["Radmap v4 2019 filtered terrestrial dose"],"knownLayerDescriptions":["Radiometric Grid of Australia (Radmap). The filtered terrestrial dose rate grid is a derivative of the 2019 radiometric or gamma-ray grid of Australia, made of a combination of over 600 individual survey grids."]}],"relatedRecords":[],"capabilityRecords":[]},{"name":"Radmap v4 2019 ratio Th over K","hidden":false,"description":"Radiometric Grid of Australia (Radmap). The thorium over potassium grid is a derivative of the 2019 radiometric or gamma-ray grid of Australia.","id":"ga-geophys-8","proxyUrl":null,"proxyGetFeatureInfoUrl":null,"proxyCountUrl":null,"proxyStyleUrl":null,"proxyDownloadUrl":null,"mapStyles":null,"feature_count":0,"singleTile":false,"legendImg":null,"previewImg":null,"group":"Geophysics - National Geophysical Compilation","layerMode":"NA","cswRecords":[{"name":"Radiometric Grid of Australia (Radmap) v4 2019 ratio thorium over potassium","resourceProvider":"Resources Division","id":"f2210_8669_1800_1509","recordInfoUrl":"https://geonetwork.nci.org.au/geonetwork/srv/eng/catalog.search#/metadata/f2210_8669_1800_1509","description":"The thorium over potassium grid is a derivative of the 2019 radiometric or gamma-ray grid of Australia. The radiometric, or gamma-ray spectrometric method, measures the natural variations in the gamma-rays detected near the Earth's surface as the result of the natural radioactive decay of potassium (K), uranium (U) and thorium (Th).  The data are collected on airborne geophysical surveys conducted by Commonwealth, State and Northern Territory Governments and the private sector.\r\nThe 2019 thorium over potassium was derived by seamlessly merging over 600 airborne gamma-ray spectrometric surveys. The final grid has a cell size of about 100m (0.001 degrees) and is derived from the filtered thorium and potassium grids.\n\n\n--\nThis record represents data published by NCI. It uses catalogue metadata modified from Geoscience Australia. See our Record Lineage Information for more details.","noCache":false,"service":false,"adminArea":null,"contactOrg":"Commonwealth of Australia (Geoscience Australia)","contactPerson":null,"funderOrg":"Unknown","authors":["Poudjom Djomani, Y.","Minty, B.R.S.","Poudjom Djomani, Y.","Poudjom Djomani, Y.","","Poudjom Djomani, Y.","Poudjom Djomani, Y.","Minty, B.R.S."],"onlineResources":[{"url":"https://gsky.nci.org.au/ows/national_geophysical_compilations?service=WMS&version=1.1.1&request=GetCapabilities","type":"WMS","name":"radmap2019_grid_thk_ratio_awags_rad_2019","description":"NCI GSKY Web Map Service (WMS)","version":"1.1.1","applicationProfile":"","protocolRequest":""},{"url":"https://gsky.nci.org.au/ows/national_geophysical_compilations?service=WCS&version=1.0.0&request=GetCapabilities","type":"WCS","name":"radmap2019_grid_thk_ratio_awags_rad_2019","description":"NCI GSKY Web Coverage Service (WCS)","version":"","applicationProfile":"","protocolRequest":""},{"url":"https://thredds.nci.org.au/thredds/fileServer/iv65/Geoscience_Australia_Geophysics_Reference_Data_Collection/national_geophysical_compilations/Radmap2019/Radmap2019-grid-thk_ratio-AWAGS_RAD_2019.nc","type":"WWW","name":"Radmap2019-grid-thk_ratio-AWAGS_RAD_2019","description":"NCI NetCDF file download via HTTP","version":"","applicationProfile":"","protocolRequest":""},{"url":"https://doi.org/10.26186/5dd48f8e542f2","type":"WWW","name":"Geoscience Australia Source Record","description":"","version":"","applicationProfile":"","protocolRequest":""}],"geographicElements":[{"type":"bbox","eastBoundLongitude":153.6715,"westBoundLongitude":112.7175,"northB