conducted by Commonwealth, State and Northern Territory Governments and the private sector.\r\nThe 2019 unfiltered uranium grid has a cell size of about 100m (0.001 degrees) and shows uranium element concentrations of the Australia region.\n\n\n--\nThis record represents data published by NCI. It uses catalogue metadata modified from Geoscience Australia. See our Record Lineage Information for more details.","noCache":false,"service":false,"adminArea":null,"contactOrg":"Commonwealth of Australia (Geoscience Australia)","contactPerson":null,"funderOrg":"Unknown","authors":["Poudjom Djomani, Y.","Minty, B.R.S.","Poudjom Djomani, Y.","Minty, B.R.S.","Poudjom Djomani, Y.","Minty, B.R.S.","Poudjom Djomani, Y.","Minty, B.R.S."],"onlineResources":[{"url":"https://gsky.nci.org.au/ows/national_geophysical_compilations?service=WMS&version=1.1.1&request=GetCapabilities","type":"WMS","name":"radmap2019_grid_u_conc_awags_rad_2019","description":"NCI GSKY Web Map Service (WMS)","version":"1.1.1","applicationProfile":"","protocolRequest":""},{"url":"https://gsky.nci.org.au/ows/national_geophysical_compilations?service=WCS&version=1.0.0&request=GetCapabilities","type":"WCS","name":"radmap2019_grid_u_conc_awags_rad_2019","description":"NCI GSKY Web Coverage Service (WCS)","version":"","applicationProfile":"","protocolRequest":""},{"url":"https://thredds.nci.org.au/thredds/fileServer/iv65/Geoscience_Australia_Geophysics_Reference_Data_Collection/national_geophysical_compilations/Radmap2019/Radmap2019-grid-u_conc-AWAGS_RAD_2019.nc","type":"WWW","name":"Radmap2019-grid-u_conc-AWAGS_RAD_2019","description":"NCI NetCDF file download via HTTP","version":"","applicationProfile":"","protocolRequest":""},{"url":"https://doi.org/10.26186/5dd4a8b28762e","type":"WWW","name":"Geoscience Australia Source Record","description":"","version":"","applicationProfile":"","protocolRequest":""}],"geographicElements":[{"type":"bbox","eastBoundLongitude":153.6715,"westBoundLongitude":112.7175,"northBoundLatitude":-9.0005,"southBoundLatitude":-43.7615}],"descriptiveKeywords":["airborne digital data",""],"datasetURIs":["10.25914/5f75661700266"],"constraints":["https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","Licences for datasets within this collection may vary. Check individual files for the relevant licence that applies.","RestrictionCode: license","Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International License"],"useLimitConstraints":["Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International License","RestrictionCode: license"],"accessConstraints":["RestrictionCode: license"],"childRecords":[],"date":"2018-04-20T00:00:00 UTC","minScale":null,"maxScale":null,"knownLayerIds":["ga-geophys-14"],"knownLayerNames":["Radmap v4 2019 unfiltered ppm U"],"knownLayerDescriptions":["Radiometric Grid of Australia (Radmap). The unfiltered uranium grid is a derivative of the 2019 radiometric or gamma-ray grid of Australia which is a merge of over 600 individual gamma-ray spectrometric surveys."]}],"relatedRecords":[],"capabilityRecords":[]},{"name":"Radmap v4 2019 unfiltered terrestrial dose","hidden":false,"description":"Radiometric Grid of Australia (Radmap). The unfiltered terrestrial dose rate grid is a derivative of the 2019 radiometric or gamma-ray grid of Australia, which is a merge of over 600 individual gamma-ray spectrometric surveys.","id":"ga-geophys-15","proxyUrl":null,"proxyGetFeatureInfoUrl":null,"proxyCountUrl":null,"proxyStyleUrl":null,"proxyDownloadUrl":null,"mapStyles":null,"feature_count":0,"singleTile":false,"legendImg":null,"previewImg":null,"group":"Geophysics - National Geophysical Compilation","layerMode":"NA","cswRecords":[{"name":"Radiometric Grid of Australia (Radmap) v4 2019 unfiltered terrestrial dose rate","resourceProvider":"Resources Division","id":"f5627_6492_9944_1058","recordInfoUrl":"https://geonetwork.nci.org.au/geonetwork/srv/eng/catalog.search#/metadata/f5627_6492_9944_1058","description":"The unfiltered terrestrial dose rate grid is a derivative of the 2019 radiometric or gamma-ray grid of Australia, which is a merge of over 600 individual gamma-ray spectrometric surveys. The radiometric, or gamma-ray spectrometric method, measures the natural variations in the gamma-rays detected near the Earth's surface as the result of the natural radioactive decay of potassium (K), uranium (U) and thorium (Th).  The data are collected on airborne geophysical surveys conducted by Commonwealth, State and Northern Territory Governments and the private sector.\r\nThe unfiltered terrestrial dose rate grid is derived as a linear combination of the unfiltered K, U and Th grids, and has a cell size of about 100m (0.001 degrees).\n\n\n--\nThis record represents data published by NCI. It uses catalogue metadata modified from Geoscience Australia. See our Record Lineage Information for more details.","noCache":false,"service":false,"adminArea":null,"contactOrg":"Commonwealth of Australia (Geoscience Australia)","contactPerson":null,"funderOrg":"Unknown","authors":["Poudjom Djomani, Y.","Minty, B.R.S.","Poudjom Djomani, Y.","Minty, B.R.S.","Poudjom Djomani, Y.","Minty, B.R.S.","Poudjom Djomani, Y.","Minty, B.R.S."],"onlineResources":[{"url":"https://gsky.nci.org.au/ows/national_geophysical_compilations?service=WMS&version=1.1.1&request=GetCapabilities","type":"WMS","name":"radmap2019_grid_dose_terr_awags_rad_2019","description":"NCI GSKY Web Map Service (WMS)","version":"1.1.1","applicationProfile":"","protocolRequest":""},{"url":"https://gsky.nci.org.au/ows/national_geophysical_compilations?service=WCS&version=1.0.0&request=GetCapabilities","type":"WCS","name":"radmap2019_grid_dose_terr_awags_rad_2019","description":"NCI GSKY Web Coverage Service (WCS)","version":"","applicationProfile":"","protocolRequest":""},{"url":"https://thredds.nci.org.au/thredds/fileServer/iv65/Geoscience_Australia_Geophysics_Reference_Data_Collection/national_geophysical_compilations/Radmap2019/Radmap2019-grid-dose_terr-AWAGS_RAD_2019.nc","type":"WWW","name":"Radmap2019-grid-dose_terr-AWAGS_RAD_2019","description":"NCI NetCDF file download via HTTP","version":"","applicationProfile":"","protocolRequest":""},{"url":"https://doi.org/10.26186/5dd4a6f76de45","type":"WWW","name":"Geoscience Australia Source Record","description":"","version":"","applicationProfile":"","protocolRequest":""}],"geographicElements":[{"type":"bbox","eastBoundLongitude":153.6715,"westBoundLongitude":112.7175,"northBoundLatitude":-9.0005,"southBoundLatitude":-43.7615}],"descriptiveKeywords":["airborne digital data",""],"datasetURIs":["10.25914/5f7564f7cad07"],"constraints":["https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","Licences for datasets within this collection may vary. Check individual files for the relevant licence that applies.","RestrictionCode: license","Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International License"],"useLimitConstraints":["Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International License","RestrictionCode: license"],"accessConstraints":["RestrictionCode: license"],"childRecords":[],"date":"2018-04-20T00:00:00 UTC","minScale":null,"maxScale":null,"knownLayerIds":["ga-geophys-15"],"knownLayerNames":["Radmap v4 2019 unfiltered terrestrial dose"],"knownLayerDescriptions":["Radiometric Grid of Australia (Radmap). The unfiltered terrestrial dose rate grid is a derivative of the 2019 radiometric or gamma-ray grid of Australia, which is a merge of over 600 individual gamma-ray spectrometric surveys."]}],"relatedRecords":[],"capabilityRecords":[]},{"name":"TMI Grid of Aust, 2019 - 7th ed. 40 m cell","hidden":false,"description":"Total magnetic intensity (TMI) data measures variations in the intensity of the Earth magnetic field caused by the contrasting content of rock-forming minerals in the Earth crust.","id":"ga-geophys-16","proxyUrl":null,"proxyGetFeatureInfoUrl":null,"proxyCountUrl":null,"proxyStyleUrl":null,"proxyDownloadUrl":null,"mapStyles":null,"feature_count":0,"singleTile":false,"legendImg":null,"previewImg":null,"group":"Geophysics - National Geophysical Compilation","layerMode":"NA","cswRecords":[{"name":"Total Magnetic Intensity (TMI) Grid of Australia 2019 - seventh edition - 40 m cell size","resourceProvider":"Unknown","id":"f1214_0762_6293_4170","recordInfoUrl":"https://geonetwork.nci.org.au/geonetwork/srv/eng/catalog.search#/metadata/f1214_0762_6293_4170","description":"Total magnetic intensity (TMI) data measures variations in the intensity of the Earth magnetic field caused by the contrasting content of rock-forming minerals in the Earth crust. Magnetic anomalies can be either positive (field stronger than normal) or negative (field weaker) depending on the susceptibility of the rock.\r\nThis grid only includes airborne-derived TMI data for onshore and near-offshore continental areas. The grid has a cell size of approximately 40 m. This spatial resolution will enable 200 m line spacing surveys incorporated into the grid to be viewed at their optimum grid resolution.\r\nSince the sixth edition was released in 2015, data from 234 new surveys have been added to the database, acquired mainly by the State and Territory Geological Surveys. The new grid was derived from a re-levelling of the national magnetic grid database. The survey grids were levelled to each other, and to the Australia Wide Airborne Geophysical Survey (AWAGS), which serves as a baseline to constrain long wavelengths in the final grid. It is estimated that 33 500 000 line-kilometres of survey data were acquired to produce the 2019 grid, about 2 000 000 line-kilometres more than for the previous edition.\n\n\n--\nThis record represents data published by NCI. It uses catalogue metadata modified from Geoscience Australia. See our Record Lineage Information for more details.","noCache":false,"service":false,"adminArea":null,"contactOrg":"Commonwealth of Australia (Geoscience Australia)","contactPerson":null,"funderOrg":"Unknown","authors":["Poudjom Djomani, Y.","Minty, B.R.S.","Poudjom Djomani, Y.","Minty, B.R.S.","Poudjom Djomani, Y.","Minty, B.R.S.","Poudjom Djomani, Y.","Minty, B.R.S."],"onlineResources":[{"url":"https://gsky.nci.org.au/ows/national_geophysical_compilations?service=WMS&version=1.1.1&request=GetCapabilities","type":"WMS","name":"magmap2019_grid_tmi_cellsize40m_awags_mag_2019","description":"NCI GSKY Web Map Service (WMS)","version":"1.1.1","applicationProfile":"","protocolRequest":""},{"url":"https://gsky.nci.org.au/ows/national_geophysical_compilations?service=WCS&version=1.0.0&request=GetCapabilities","type":"WCS","name":"magmap2019_grid_tmi_cellsize40m_awags_mag_2019","description":"NCI GSKY Web Coverage Service (WCS)","version":"","applicationProfile":"","protocolRequest":""},{"url":"https://thredds.nci.org.au/thredds/fileServer/iv65/Geoscience_Australia_Geophysics_Reference_Data_Collection/national_geophysical_compilations/Magmap2019/Magmap2019-grid-tmi-Cellsize40m-AWAGS_MAG_2019.nc","type":"WWW","name":"Magmap2019-grid-tmi-Cellsize40m-AWAGS_MAG_2019","description":"NCI NetCDF file download via HTTP","version":"","applicationProfile":"","protocolRequest":""},{"url":"https://doi.org/10.26186/5dd5fb557fffb","type":"WWW","name":"Geoscience Australia Source Record","description":"","version":"","applicationProfile":"","protocolRequest":""}],"geographicElements":[{"type":"bbox","eastBoundLongitude":154.662516,"westBoundLongitude":112.502532,"northBoundLatitude":-9.025662,"southBoundLatitude":-43.928981}],"descriptiveKeywords":["TMI",""],"datasetURIs":["10.25914/5f756475c7fea"],"constraints":["https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","Licences for datasets within this collection may vary. Check individual files for the relevant licence that applies.","RestrictionCode: license","Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International License"],"useLimitConstraints":["Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International License","RestrictionCode: license"],"accessConstraints":["RestrictionCode: license"],"childRecords":[],"date":"2018-04-20T00:00:00 UTC","minScale":null,"maxScale":null,"knownLayerIds":["ga-geophys-16"],"knownLayerNames":["TMI Grid of Aust, 2019 - 7th ed. 40 m cell"],"knownLayerDescriptions":["Total magnetic intensity (TMI) data measures variations in the intensity of the Earth magnetic field caused by the contrasting content of rock-forming minerals in the Earth crust."]}],"relatedRecords":[],"capabilityRecords":[]},{"name":"TMI Grid of Aust, 2019 - 7th ed. 80 m cell","hidden":false,"description":"Total magnetic intensity (TMI) data measures variations in the intensity of the Earth magnetic field caused by the contrasting content of rock-forming minerals in the Earth crust.","id":"ga-geophys-17","proxyUrl":null,"proxyGetFeatureInfoUrl":null,"proxyCountUrl":null,"proxyStyleUrl":null,"proxyDownloadUrl":null,"mapStyles":null,"feature_count":0,"singleTile":false,"legendImg":null,"previewImg":null,"group":"Geophysics - National Geophysical Compilation","layerMode":"NA","cswRecords":[{"name":"Total Magnetic Intensity (TMI) Grid of Australia 2019 - seventh edition - 80 m cell size","resourceProvider":"Resources Division","id":"f4282_0088_0223_5551","recordInfoUrl":"https://geonetwork.nci.org.au/geonetwork/srv/eng/catalog.search#/metadata/f4282_0088_0223_5551","description":"Total magnetic intensity (TMI) data measures variations in the intensity of the Earth magnetic field caused by the contrasting content of rock-forming minerals in the Earth crust. Magnetic anomalies can be either positive (field stronger than normal) or negative (field weaker) depending on the susceptibility of the rock.\r\nThe 2019 Total magnetic Intensity (TMI) grid of Australia has a grid cell size of ~3 seconds of arc (approximately 80 m). This grid only includes airborne-derived TMI data for onshore and near-offshore continental areas.\r\nSince the sixth edition was released in 2015, data from 234 new surveys have been added to the database, acquired mainly by the State and Territory Geological Surveys. The new grid was derived from a re-levelling of the national magnetic grid database. The survey grids were levelled to each other, and to the Australia Wide Airborne Geophysical Survey (AWAGS), which serves as a baseline to constrain long wavelengths in the final grid. It is estimated that 33 500 000 line-kilometres of survey data were acquired to produce the 2019 grid data, about 2 000 000 line-kilometres more than for the previous edition.\n\n\n--\nThis record represents data published by NCI. It uses catalogue metadata modified from Geoscience Australia. See our Record Lineage Information for more details.","noCache":false,"service":false,"adminArea":null,"contactOrg":"Commonwealth of Australia (Geoscience Australia)","contactPerson":null,"funderOrg":"Unknown","authors":["Poudjom Djomani, Y.","Minty, B.R.S.","Hutchens, M.","Lane, R.J.L.","Poudjom Djomani, Y.","Minty, B.R.S.","Hutchens, M.","Lane, R.J.L.","Poudjom Djomani, Y.","Minty, B.R.S.","Hutchens, M.","Lane, R.J.L.","Poudjom Djomani, Y.","Minty, B.R.S.","Hutchens, M.","Lane, R.J.L."],"onlineResources":[{"url":"https://gsky.nci.org.au/ows/national_geophysical_compilations?service=WMS&version=1.1.1&request=GetCapabilities","type":"WMS","name":"magmap2019_grid_tmi_awags_mag_2019","description":"NCI GSKY Web Map Service (WMS)","version":"1.1.1","applicationProfile":"","protocolRequest":""},{"url":"https://gsky.nci.org.au/ows/national_geophysical_compilations?service=WCS&version=1.0.0&request=GetCapabilities","type":"WCS","name":"magmap2019_grid_tmi_awags_mag_2019","description":"NCI GSKY Web Coverage Service (WCS)","version":"","applicationProfile":"","protocolRequest":""},{"url":"https://thredds.nci.org.au/thredds/fileServer/iv65/Geoscience_Australia_Geophysics_Reference_Data_Collection/national_geophysical_compilations/Magmap2019/Magmap2019-grid-tmi-AWAGS_MAG_2019.nc","type":"WWW","name":"Magmap2019-grid-tmi-AWAGS_MAG_2019","description":"NCI NetCDF file download via HTTP","version":"","applicationProfile":"","protocolRequest":""},{"url":"https://doi.org/10.26186/5e9cf3f2c0f1d","type":"WWW","name":"Geoscience Australia Source Record","description":"","version":"","applicationProfile":"","protocolRequest":""}],"geographicElements":[{"type":"bbox","eastBoundLongitude":154.662516,"westBoundLongitude":112.502532,"northBoundLatitude":-9.025662,"southBoundLatitude":-43.928981}],"descriptiveKeywords":["TMI",""],"datasetURIs":["10.25914/5f756440af920"],"constraints":["https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","Licences for datasets within this collection may vary. Check individual files for the relevant licence that applies.","RestrictionCode: license","Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International License"],"useLimitConstraints":["Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International License","RestrictionCode: license"],"accessConstraints":["RestrictionCode: license"],"childRecords":[],"date":"2018-04-20T00:00:00 UTC","minScale":null,"maxScale":null,"knownLayerIds":["ga-geophys-17"],"knownLayerNames":["TMI Grid of Aust, 2019 - 7th ed. 80 m cell"],"knownLayerDescriptions":["Total magnetic intensity (TMI) data measures variations in the intensity of the Earth magnetic field caused by the contrasting content of rock-forming minerals in the Earth crust."]}],"relatedRecords":[],"capabilityRecords":[]},{"name":"TMI Grid of Aust. 2019 - VRTP 7th ed.","hidden":false,"description":"The 2019 Total magnetic Intensity (TMI) grid of Australia with variable reduction to pole (VRTP) has a grid cell size of ~3 seconds of arc (approximately 80 m). This grid only includes airborne-derived TMI data for onshore and near-offshore continental areas.","id":"ga-geophys-18","proxyUrl":null,"proxyGetFeatureInfoUrl":null,"proxyCountUrl":null,"proxyStyleUrl":null,"proxyDownloadUrl":null,"mapStyles":null,"feature_count":0,"singleTile":false,"legendImg":null,"previewImg":null,"group":"Geophysics - National Geophysical Compilation","layerMode":"NA","cswRecords":[{"name":"Total Magnetic Intensity (TMI) Grid of Australia with Variable Reduction to Pole (VRTP) 2019 - seventh edition","resourceProvider":"Resources Division","id":"f3019_9432_3181_9424","recordInfoUrl":"https://geonetwork.nci.org.au/geonetwork/srv/eng/catalog.search#/metadata/f3019_9432_3181_9424","description":"Total magnetic intensity (TMI) data measures variations in the intensity of the Earth magnetic field caused by the contrasting content of rock-forming minerals in the Earth crust. Magnetic anomalies can be either positive (field stronger than normal) or negative (field weaker) depending on the susceptibility of the rock. A variable reduction to Pole is aimed at locating magnetic anomalies exactly above their source bodies and without any distortion. The 2019 Total magnetic Intensity (TMI) grid of Australia with variable reduction to pole (VRTP) has a grid cell size of ~3 seconds of arc (approximately 80 m). This grid only includes airborne-derived TMI data for onshore and near-offshore continental areas. The VRTP processing followed a differential reduction to pole calculation up to 5th order polynomial. Magnetic inclination and declination were derived from the IGRF-11 geomagnetic reference model using a data representative date of January 2005 and elevation 300 m.\n\n\n--\nThis record represents data published by NCI. It uses catalogue metadata modified from Geoscience Australia. See our Record Lineage Information for more details.","noCache":false,"service":false,"adminArea":null,"contactOrg":"Commonwealth of Australia (Geoscience Australia)","contactPerson":null,"funderOrg":"Unknown","authors":["Poudjom Djomani, Y.","Minty, B.R.S.","Poudjom Djomani, Y.","Minty, B.R.S.","Poudjom Djomani, Y.","Minty, B.R.S.","Poudjom Djomani, Y.","Minty, B.R.S."],"onlineResources":[{"url":"https://gsky.nci.org.au/ows/national_geophysical_compilations?service=WMS&version=1.1.1&request=GetCapabilities","type":"WMS","name":"magmap2019_grid_tmi_rtp_awags_mag_2019","description":"NCI GSKY Web Map Service (WMS)","version":"1.1.1","applicationProfile":"","protocolRequest":""},{"url":"https://gsky.nci.org.au/ows/national_geophysical_compilations?service=WCS&version=1.0.0&request=GetCapabilities","type":"WCS","name":"magmap2019_grid_tmi_rtp_awags_mag_2019","description":"NCI GSKY Web Coverage Service (WCS)","version":"","applicationProfile":"","protocolRequest":""},{"url":"https://thredds.nci.org.au/thredds/fileServer/iv65/Geoscience_Australia_Geophysics_Reference_Data_Collection/national_geophysical_compilations/Magmap2019/Magmap2019-grid-tmi_rtp-AWAGS_MAG_2019.nc","type":"WWW","name":"Magmap2019-grid-tmi_rtp-AWAGS_MAG_2019","description":"NCI NetCDF file download via HTTP","version":"","applicationProfile":"","protocolRequest":""},{"url":"https://doi.org/10.26186/5e9cf2e3477e8","type":"WWW","name":"Geoscience Australia Source Record","description":"","version":"","applicationProfile":"","protocolRequest":""}],"geographicElements":[{"type":"bbox","eastBoundLongitude":154.661682,"westBoundLongitude":112.502532,"northBoundLatitude":-9.025662,"southBoundLatitude":-43.927315}],"descriptiveKeywords":["RTP",""],"datasetURIs":["10.25914/5f7564adc0c8a"],"constraints":["https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","Licences for datasets within this collection may vary. Check individual files for the relevant licence that applies.","RestrictionCode: license","Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International License"],"useLimitConstraints":["Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International License","RestrictionCode: license"],"accessConstraints":["RestrictionCode: license"],"childRecords":[],"date":"2018-04-20T00:00:00 UTC","minScale":null,"maxScale":null,"knownLayerIds":["ga-geophys-18"],"knownLayerNames":["TMI Grid of Aust. 2019 - VRTP 7th ed."],"knownLayerDescriptions":["The 2019 Total magnetic Intensity (TMI) grid of Australia with variable reduction to pole (VRTP) has a grid cell size of ~3 seconds of arc (approximately 80 m). This grid only includes airborne-derived TMI data for onshore and near-offshore continental areas."]}],"relatedRecords":[],"capabilityRecords":[]},{"name":"TMI Grid of Aust. 2019 - 1VD","hidden":false,"description":"The first vertical derivative (1VD) grid is derived from the 2019 Total magnetic Intensity (TMI) grid of Australia which has a grid cell size of ~3 seconds of arc (approximately 80 m).","id":"ga-geophys-19","proxyUrl":null,"proxyGetFeatureInfoUrl":null,"proxyCountUrl":null,"proxyStyleUrl":null,"proxyDownloadUrl":null,"mapStyles":null,"feature_count":0,"singleTile":false,"legendImg":null,"previewImg":null,"group":"Geophysics - National Geophysical Compilation","layerMode":"NA","cswRecords":[{"name":"Total Magnetic Intensity Grid of Australia 2019 - First Vertical Derivative (1VD)","resourceProvider":"Resources Division","id":"f2640_4876_3438_2505","recordInfoUrl":"https://geonetwork.nci.org.au/geonetwork/srv/eng/catalog.search#/metadata/f2640_4876_3438_2505","description":"Total magnetic intensity (TMI) data measures variations in the intensity of the Earth magnetic field caused by the contrasting content of rock-forming minerals in the Earth crust. Magnetic anomalies can be either positive (field stronger than normal) or negative (field weaker) depending on the susceptibility of the rock.\r\nThe first vertical derivative (1VD) grid is derived from the 2019 Total magnetic Intensity (TMI) grid of Australia which has a grid cell size of ~3 seconds of arc (approximately 80 m). As the vertical derivative filter is essentially a high-pass filter, longer wavelengths are suppressed, and shorter wavelengths emphasized. The magnetic units of the data are in nT per metre.\n\n\n--\nThis record represents data published by NCI. It uses catalogue metadata modified from Geoscience Australia. See our Record Lineage Information for more details.","noCache":false,"service":false,"adminArea":null,"contactOrg":"Commonwealth of Australia (Geoscience Australia)","contactPerson":null,"funderOrg":"Unknown","authors":["Poudjom Djomani, Y.","Minty, B.R.S.","Poudjom Djomani, Y.","Minty, B.R.S.","Poudjom Djomani, Y.","Minty, B.R.S.","Poudjom Djomani, Y.","Minty, B.R.S."],"onlineResources":[{"url":"https://gsky.nci.org.au/ows/national_geophysical_compilations?service=WMS&version=1.1.1&request=GetCapabilities","type":"WMS","name":"magmap2019_grid_tmi_1vd_awags_mag_2019","description":"NCI GSKY Web Map Service (WMS)","version":"1.1.1","applicationProfile":"","protocolRequest":""},{"url":"https://gsky.nci.org.au/ows/national_geophysical_compilations?service=WCS&version=1.0.0&request=GetCapabilities","type":"WCS","name":"magmap2019_grid_tmi_1vd_awags_mag_2019","description":"NCI GSKY Web Coverage Service (WCS)","version":"","applicationProfile":"","protocolRequest":""},{"url":"https://thredds.nci.org.au/thredds/fileServer/iv65/Geoscience_Australia_Geophysics_Reference_Data_Collection/national_geophysical_compilations/Magmap2019/Magmap2019-grid-tmi_1vd-AWAGS_MAG_2019.nc","type":"WWW","name":"Magmap2019-grid-tmi_1vd-AWAGS_MAG_2019","description":"NCI NetCDF file download via HTTP","version":"","applicationProfile":"","protocolRequest":""},{"url":"https://doi.org/10.26186/5dd48b1368ece","type":"WWW","name":"Geoscience Australia Source Record","description":"","version":"","applicationProfile":"","protocolRequest":""}],"geographicElements":[{"type":"bbox","eastBoundLongitude":154.662516,"westBoundLongitude":112.502532,"northBoundLatitude":-9.025662,"southBoundLatitude":-43.928981}],"descriptiveKeywords":["Vertical Derivative",""],"datasetURIs":["10.25914/5f75640aae140"],"constraints":["https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","Licences for datasets within this collection may vary. Check individual files for the relevant licence that applies.","RestrictionCode: license","Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International License"],"useLimitConstraints":["Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International License","RestrictionCode: license"],"accessConstraints":["RestrictionCode: license"],"childRecords":[],"date":"2018-04-20T00:00:00 UTC","minScale":null,"maxScale":null,"knownLayerIds":["ga-geophys-19"],"knownLayerNames":["TMI Grid of Aust. 2019 - 1VD"],"knownLayerDescriptions":["The first vertical derivative (1VD) grid is derived from the 2019 Total magnetic Intensity (TMI) grid of Australia which has a grid cell size of ~3 seconds of arc (approximately 80 m)."]}],"relatedRecords":[],"capabilityRecords":[]},{"name":"AlOH group composition","hidden":false,"description":"1. Band ratio: B5/B7Blue is well ordered kaolinite, Al-rich muscovite/illite, paragonite, pyrophyllite Red is Al-poor Si-rich) muscovite phengite)","id":"aster-aloh","proxyUrl":null,"proxyGetFeatureInfoUrl":null,"proxyCountUrl":null,"proxyStyleUrl":null,"proxyDownloadUrl":null,"mapStyles":null,"feature_count":0,"singleTile":false,"legendImg":null,"previewImg":null,"group":"ASTER Mineral Maps","layerMode":"NA","cswRecords":[{"name":"National ASTER Map AlOH group composition","resourceProvider":"Resources Division","id":"f1823_6337_2787_1326","recordInfoUrl":"https://geonetwork.nci.org.au/geonetwork/srv/eng/catalog.search#/metadata/f1823_6337_2787_1326","description":"1. Band ratio: B5/B7 Blue is well ordered kaolinite, Al-rich muscovite/illite, paragonite, pyrophyllite Red is Al-poor (Si-rich) muscovite (phengite)\r\nuseful for mapping: (1) exposed saprolite/saprock is often white mica or Al-smectite (warmer colours) whereas transported materials are often kaolin-rich (cooler colours); (2) clays developed over carbonates, especially Al-smectite (montmorillonite, beidellite) will produce middle to warmers colours. (2) stratigraphic mapping based on different clay-types; and (3) lithology-overprinting hydrothermal alteration, e.g. Si-rich and K-rich phengitic mica (warmer colours). Combine with Ferrous iron in MgOH and FeOH content products to look for evidence of overlapping/juxtaposed potassic metasomatism in ferromagnesian parents rocks (e.g. Archaean greenstone associated Au mineralisation) +/- associated distal propyllitic alteration (e.g. chlorite, amphibole).\n\n\n--\nThis record represents data published by NCI. It uses catalogue metadata modified from Geoscience Australia. See our Record Lineage Information for more details.","noCache":false,"service":false,"adminArea":null,"contactOrg":"Commonwealth Scientific & Industrial Research Organisation (CSIRO)","contactPerson":"Cudahy, T.","funderOrg":"Unknown","authors":["Cudahy, T.","Caccetta, M.","Lau, I.","Rodger, A.","Laukamp, C.","Ong, C.","Chia, J.","Collings, S.","Rankine, T.","Fraser, R.","Woodcock, R.","Vote, J.","Warren, P.","Thomas, M.","Tyler, I.","Mauger, A.","Close, D.","Jones, M.","Abrams, M.","Cudahy, T.","Caccetta, M.","Lau, I.","Rodger, A.","Laukamp, C.","Ong, C.","Chia, J.","Collings, S.","Rankine, T.","Fraser, R.","Woodcock, R.","Vote, J.","Warren, P.","Thomas, M.","Tyler, I.","Mauger, A.","Close, D.","Jones, M.","Abrams, M.","Cudahy, T.","Caccetta, M.","Lau, I.","Rodger, A.","Laukamp, C.","Ong, C.","Chia, J.","Collings, S.","Rankine, T.","Fraser, R.","Woodcock, R.","Vote, J.","Warren, P.","Thomas, M.","Tyler, I.","Mauger, A.","Close, D.","Jones, M.","Abrams, M.","Cudahy, T.","Caccetta, M.","Lau, I.","Rodger, A.","Laukamp, C.","Ong, C.","Chia, J.","Collings, S.","Rankine, T.","Fraser, R.","Woodcock, R.","Vote, J.","Warren, P.","Thomas, M.","Tyler, I.","Mauger, A.","Close, D.","Jones, M.","Abrams, M."],"onlineResources":[{"url":"https://gsky.nci.org.au/ows/aster?service=WMS&version=1.1.1&request=GetCapabilities","type":"WMS","name":"AlOH_Group_Composition","description":"NCI GSKY Web Map Service (WMS)","version":"1.1.1","applicationProfile":"","protocolRequest":""},{"url":"https://gsky.nci.org.au/ows/aster?service=WCS&version=1.0.0&request=GetCapabilities","type":"WCS","name":"AlOH_Group_Composition","description":"NCI GSKY Web Coverage Service (WCS)","version":"","applicationProfile":"","protocolRequest":""},{"url":"https://thredds.nci.org.au/thredds/dodsC/wx7/aster/vnir/Aus_Mainland/Aus_Mainland_AlOH_group_composition_reprojected.nc4.html","type":"Unsupported","name":"AlOH_g