includes: chlorite, epidote, jarosite, nontronite, gibbsite, gypsum, opal-chalcedony)"]}],"relatedRecords":[],"capabilityRecords":[]},{"name":"Ferric oxide composition","hidden":false,"description":"1. Band ratio: B2/B1Blue-cyan is goethite rich, Green is hematite-goethite, Red-yellow is hematite-rich","id":"aster-ferric-oxide-comp","proxyUrl":null,"proxyGetFeatureInfoUrl":null,"proxyCountUrl":null,"proxyStyleUrl":null,"proxyDownloadUrl":null,"mapStyles":null,"feature_count":0,"singleTile":false,"legendImg":null,"previewImg":null,"group":"ASTER Mineral Maps","layerMode":"NA","cswRecords":[{"name":"National ASTER Map Ferric oxide composition","resourceProvider":"Resources Division","id":"f7401_6489_2308_2725","recordInfoUrl":"https://geonetwork.nci.org.au/geonetwork/srv/eng/catalog.search#/metadata/f7401_6489_2308_2725","description":"1. Band ratio: B2/B1 Blue-cyan is goethite rich, Green is hematite-goethite, Red-yellow is hematite-rich\r\n(1) Mapping transported materials (including palaeochannels) characterised by hematite (relative to geothite). Combine with AlOH composition to find co-located areas of hematite and poorly ordered kaolin to map transported materials; and (2) hematite-rish areas in drier conditions (eg above the water table) whereas goethite-rich in wetter conditions (eg at/below the water or areas recently exposed). May also be climate driven.\n\n\n--\nThis record represents data published by NCI. It uses catalogue metadata modified from Geoscience Australia. See our Record Lineage Information for more details.","noCache":false,"service":false,"adminArea":null,"contactOrg":"Commonwealth Scientific & Industrial Research Organisation (CSIRO)","contactPerson":"Cudahy, T.","funderOrg":"Unknown","authors":["Cudahy, T.","Caccetta, M.","Lau, I.","Rodger, A.","Laukamp, C.","Ong, C.","Chia, J.","Collings, S.","Rankine, T.","Fraser, R.","Woodcock, R.","Vote, J.","Warren, P.","Thomas, M.","Tyler, I.","Mauger, A.","Close, D.","Jones, M.","Abrams, M.","Cudahy,