nd ratio: B2/B1Blue-cyan is goethite rich, Green is hematite-goethite, Red-yellow is hematite-rich"]}],"relatedRecords":[],"capabilityRecords":[]},{"name":"Kaolin group index","hidden":false,"description":"B6/B5(potential includes: pyrophyllite, alunite, well-ordered kaolinite)Blue is low content, Red is high content","id":"aster-group-index","proxyUrl":null,"proxyGetFeatureInfoUrl":null,"proxyCountUrl":null,"proxyStyleUrl":null,"proxyDownloadUrl":null,"mapStyles":null,"feature_count":0,"singleTile":false,"legendImg":null,"previewImg":null,"group":"ASTER Mineral Maps","layerMode":"NA","cswRecords":[{"name":"National ASTER Map Kaolin group index","resourceProvider":"Resources Division","id":"f9063_0048_5432_4205","recordInfoUrl":"https://geonetwork.nci.org.au/geonetwork/srv/eng/catalog.search#/metadata/f9063_0048_5432_4205","description":"B6/B5 (potential includes: pyrophyllite, alunite, well-ordered kaolinite) Blue is low content, Red is high content\r\nUseful for mapping: (1) different clay-type stratigraphic horizons; (2) lithology-overprinting hydrothermal alteration, e.g. high sulphidation, \"advanced argillic\" alteration comprising pyrophyllite, alunite, kaolinite/dickite; and (3) well-ordered kaolinite (warmer colours) versus poorly-ordered kaolinite (cooler colours) which can be used for mapping in situ versus transported materials, respectively.\n\n\n--\nThis record represents data published by NCI. It uses catalogue metadata modified from Geoscience Australia. See our Record Lineage Information for more details.","noCache":false,"service":false,"adminArea":null,"contactOrg":"Commonwealth Scientific & Industrial Research Organisation (CSIRO)","contactPerson":"Cudahy, T.","funderOrg":"Unknown","authors":["Cudahy, T.","Caccetta, M.","Lau, I.","Rodger, A.","Laukamp, C.","Ong, C.","Chia, J.","Collings, S.","Rankine, T.","Fraser, R.","Woodcock, R.","Vote, J.","Warren, P.","Thomas, M.","Tyler, I.","Mauger, A.","Close, D.","Jones, M.","Abrams, M.","Cudahy, T.","Ca