ion_content","description":"NCI OPeNDAP landing page - Tasmania","version":"","applicationProfile":"","protocolRequest":""},{"url":"https://thredds.nci.org.au/thredds/ncss/grid/wx7/aster/vnir/Aus_Mainland/Aus_Mainland_Green_vegetation_content_reprojected.nc4/dataset.html","type":"WWW","name":"Green_vegetation_content","description":"NCI NetCDF Subset Service - mainland Australia","version":"","applicationProfile":"","protocolRequest":""},{"url":"https://thredds.nci.org.au/thredds/ncss/grid/wx7/aster/vnir/Tasmania/Tas_Green_Vegetation_Content_reprojected.nc4/dataset.html","type":"WWW","name":"Green_vegetation_content","description":"NCI NetCDF Subset Service - Tasmania","version":"","applicationProfile":"","protocolRequest":""},{"url":"https://thredds.nci.org.au/thredds/fileServer/wx7/aster/vnir/Aus_Mainland/Aus_Mainland_Green_vegetation_content_reprojected.nc4","type":"WWW","name":"Green_vegetation_content","description":"NCI NetCDF file download via HTTP - mainland Australia","version":"","applicationProfile":"","protocolRequest":""},{"url":"https://thredds.nci.org.au/thredds/fileServer/wx7/aster/vnir/Tasmania/Tas_Green_Vegetation_Content_reprojected.nc4","type":"WWW","name":"Green_vegetation_content","description":"NCI NetCDF file download via HTTP - Tasmania","version":"","applicationProfile":"","protocolRequest":""},{"url":"https://doi.org/10.4225/08/51400D6F7B335","type":"WWW","name":"CSIRO Data Access Portal Record","description":"","version":"","applicationProfile":"","protocolRequest":""}],"geographicElements":[{"type":"bbox","eastBoundLongitude":155.0,"westBoundLongitude":111.5,"northBoundLatitude":-9.0,"southBoundLatitude":-44.5}],"descriptiveKeywords":["Earth Sciences",""],"datasetURIs":["10.25914/5f224f02a595f"],"constraints":["https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","RestrictionCode: restricted","Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International","RestrictionCode: license"],"useLimitConstraints":["Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International","RestrictionCode: license"],"accessConstraints":["RestrictionCode: restricted"],"childRecords":[],"date":"2018-04-11T00:00:00 UTC","minScale":null,"maxScale":null,"knownLayerIds":["aster-green-veg"],"knownLayerNames":["Green vegetation content"],"knownLayerDescriptions":["Band ratio: B3/B2 Blue is low contentRed is high content"]}],"relatedRecords":[],"capabilityRecords":[]},{"name":"Ferrous iron content in MgOH/carbonate","hidden":false,"description":"1. Band ratio: B5/B4Blue is low ferrous iron content in carbonate and MgOH minerals like talc and tremolite.Red is high ferrous iron content in carbonate and MgOH minerals like chlorite and actinolite.","id":"aster-ferr-carb","proxyUrl":null,"proxyGetFeatureInfoUrl":null,"proxyCountUrl":null,"proxyStyleUrl":null,"proxyDownloadUrl":null,"mapStyles":null,"feature_count":0,"singleTile":false,"legendImg":null,"previewImg":null,"group":"ASTER Mineral Maps","layerMode":"NA","cswRecords":[{"name":"National ASTER Map Ferrous iron content in MgOH/carbonate","resourceProvider":"Resources Division","id":"f2024_0154_4178_4072","recordInfoUrl":"https://geonetwork.nci.org.au/geonetwork/srv/eng/catalog.search#/metadata/f2024_0154_4178_4072","description":"1. Band ratio: B5/B4 Blue is low ferrous iron content in carbonate and MgOH minerals like talc and tremolite. Red is high ferrous iron content in carbonate and MgOH minerals like chlorite and actinolite.\r\nUseful for mapping: (1) un-oxidised \"parent rocks\" - i.e. mapping exposed parent rock materials (warm colours) in transported cover; (2) talc/tremolite (Mg-rich - cool colours) versus actinolite (Fe-rich - warm colours); (3) ferrous-bearing carbonates (warm colours) potentially associated with metasomatic \"alteration\"; (4) calcite/dolomite which are ferrous iron-poor (cool colours); and (5) epidote, which is ferrous iron poor (cool colours) - in combination with FeOH content product (high).\n\n\n--\nThis record represents data published by NCI. It uses catalogue metadata modified from Geoscience Australia. See our Record Lineage Information for more details.","noCache":false,"service":false,"adminArea":null,"contactOrg":"Commonwealth Scientific & Industrial Research Organisation (CSIRO)","contactPerson":"Cudahy, T.","funderOrg":"Unknown","authors":["Cudahy, T.","Caccetta, M.","Lau, I.","Rodger, A.","Laukamp, C.","Ong, C.","Chia, J.","Collings, S.","Rankine, T.","Fraser, R.","Woodcock, R.","Vote, J.","Warren, P.","Thomas, M.","Tyler, I.","Mauger, A.","Close, D.","Jones, M.","Abrams, M.","Cudahy, T.","Caccetta, M.","Lau, I.","Rodger, A.","Laukamp, C.","Ong, C.","Chia, J.","Collings, S.","Rankine, T.","Fraser, R.","Woodcock, R.","Vote, J.","Warren, P.","Thomas, M.","Tyler, I.","Mauger, A.","Close, D.","Jones, M.","Abrams, M.","Cudahy, T.","Caccetta, M.","Lau, I.","Rodger, A.","Laukamp, C.","Ong, C.","Chia, J.","Collings, S.","Rankine, T.","Fraser, R.","Woodcock, R.","Vote, J.","Warren, P.","Thomas, M.","Tyler, I.","Mauger, A.","Close, D.","Jones, M.","Abrams, M.","Cudahy, T.","Caccetta, M.","Lau, I.","Rodger, A.","Laukamp, C.","Ong, C.","Chia, J.","Collings, S.","Rankine, T.","Fraser, R.","Woodcock, R.","Vote, J.","Warren, P.","Thomas, M.","Tyler, I.","Mauger, A.","Close, D.","Jones, M.","Abrams, M."],"onlineResources":[{"url":"https://gsky.nci.org.au/ows/aster?service=WMS&version=1.1.1&request=GetCapabilities","type":"WMS","name":"Ferrous_Iron_in_MgOH","description":"NCI GSKY Web Map Service (WMS)","version":"1.1.1","applicationProfile":"","protocolRequest":""},{"url":"https://gsky.nci.org.au/ows/aster?service=WCS&version=1.0.0&request=GetCapabilities","type":"WCS","name":"Ferrous_Iron_in_MgOH","description":"NCI GSKY Web Coverage Service (WCS)","version":"","applicationProfile":"","protocolRequest":""},{"url":"https://thredds.nci.org.au/thredds/dodsC/wx7/aster/vnir/Tasmania/Tas_Ferrous_iron_in_MgOH_content_reprojected.nc4.html","type":"Unsupported","name":"Ferrous_iron_content_in_MgOH","description":"NCI OPeNDAP landing page - Tasmania","version":"","applicationProfile":"","protocolRequest":""},{"url":"https://thredds.nci.org.au/thredds/ncss/grid/wx7/aster/vnir/Tasmania/Tas_Ferrous_iron_in_MgOH_content_reprojected.nc4/dataset.html","type":"WWW","name":"Ferrous_iron_content_in_MgOH","description":"NCI NetCDF Subset Service - Tasmania","version":"","applicationProfile":"","protocolRequest":""},{"url":"https://thredds.nci.org.au/thredds/fileServer/wx7/aster/vnir/Tasmania/Tas_Ferrous_iron_in_MgOH_content_reprojected.nc4","type":"WWW","name":"Ferrous_iron_content_in_MgOH","description":"NCI NetCDF file download via HTTP - Tasmania","version":"","applicationProfile":"","protocolRequest":""},{"url":"https://doi.org/10.4225/08/51400D6F7B335","type":"WWW","name":"CSIRO Data Access Portal Record","description":"","version":"","applicationProfile":"","protocolRequest":""}],"geographicElements":[{"type":"bbox","eastBoundLongitude":155.0,"westBoundLongitude":111.5,"northBoundLatitude":-9.0,"southBoundLatitude":-44.5}],"descriptiveKeywords":["Earth Sciences",""],"datasetURIs":["10.25914/5f224f1f2236f"],"constraints":["https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","RestrictionCode: restricted","Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International","RestrictionCode: license"],"useLimitConstraints":["Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International","RestrictionCode: license"],"accessConstraints":["RestrictionCode: restricted"],"childRecords":[],"date":"2018-04-10T00:00:00 UTC","minScale":null,"maxScale":null,"knownLayerIds":["aster-ferr-carb"],"knownLayerNames":["Ferrous iron content in MgOH/carbonate"],"knownLayerDescriptions":["1. Band ratio: B5/B4Blue is low ferrous iron content in carbonate and MgOH minerals like talc and tremolite.Red is high ferrous iron content in carbonate and MgOH minerals like chlorite and actinolite."]}],"relatedRecords":[],"capabilityRecords":[]},{"name":"MgOH group composition","hidden":false,"description":"1. Band ratio: B7/B8Blue-cyan is magnesite-dolomite, amphibole, chlorite\tRed is calcite, epidote, amphibole","id":"aster-mgoh-group-comp","proxyUrl":null,"proxyGetFeatureInfoUrl":null,"proxyCountUrl":null,"proxyStyleUrl":null,"proxyDownloadUrl":null,"mapStyles":null,"feature_count":0,"singleTile":false,"legendImg":null,"previewImg":null,"group":"ASTER Mineral Maps","geojson":{"bbox":[[143.1,-43.9],[149.0,-39.3]]},"layerMode":"NA","cswRecords":[{"name":"National ASTER Map MgOH group composition","resourceProvider":"Resources Division","id":"f4127_0310_8856_3869","recordInfoUrl":"https://geonetwork.nci.org.au/geonetwork/srv/eng/catalog.search#/metadata/f4127_0310_8856_3869","description":"1. Band ratio: B7/B8 Blue-cyan is magnesite-dolomite, amphibole, chlorite Red is calcite, epidote, amphibole\r\nuseful for mapping: (1) exposed parent material persisting through \"cover\"; (2) \"dolomitization\" alteration in carbonates - combine with Ferrous iron in MgOH product to help separate dolomite versus ankerite; (3) lithology-cutting hydrothermal (e.g. propyllitic) alteration - combine with FeOH content product and ferrous iron in Mg-OH to isolate chlorite from actinolite versus talc versus epidote; and (4) layering within mafic/ultramafic intrusives. useful for mapping: (1) exposed parent material persisting through \"cover\"; (2) \"dolomitization\" alteration in carbonates - combine with Ferrous iron in MgOH product to help separate dolomite versus ankerite; (3) lithology-cutting hydrothermal (e.g. propyllitic) alteration - combine with FeOH content product and ferrous iron in Mg-OH to isolate chlorite from actinolite versus talc versus epidote; and (4) layering within mafic/ultramafic intrusives. useful for mapping: (1) exposed parent material persisting through \"cover\"; (2) \"dolomitization\" alteration in carbonates - combine with Ferrous iron in MgOH product to help separate dolomite versus ankerite; (3) lithology-cutting hydrothermal (e.g. propyllitic) alteration - combine with FeOH content product and ferrous iron in Mg-OH to isolate chlorite from actinolite versus talc versus epidote; and (4) layering within mafic/ultramafic intrusives.\n\n\n--\nThis record represents data published by NCI. It uses catalogue metadata modified from Geoscience Australia. See our Record Lineage Information for more details.","noCache":false,"service":false,"adminArea":null,"contactOrg":"Commonwealth Scientific & Industrial Research Organisation (CSIRO)","contactPerson":"Cudahy, T.","funderOrg":"Unknown","authors":["Cudahy, T.","Caccetta, M.","Lau, I.","Rodger, A.","Laukamp, C.","Ong, C.","Chia, J.","Collings, S.","Rankine, T.","Fraser, R.","Woodcock, R.","Vote, J.","Warren, P.","Thomas, M.","Tyler, I.","Mauger, A.","Close, D.","Jones, M.","Abrams, M.","Cudahy, T.","Caccetta, M.","Lau, I.","Rodger, A.","Laukamp, C.","Ong, C.","Chia, J.","Collings, S.","Rankine, T.","Fraser, R.","Woodcock, R.","Vote, J.","Warren, P.","Thomas, M.","Tyler, I.","Mauger, A.","Close, D.","Jones, M.","Abrams, M.","Cudahy, T.","Caccetta, M.","Lau, I.","Rodger, A.","Laukamp, C.","Ong, C.","Chia, J.","Collings, S.","Rankine, T.","Fraser, R.","Woodcock, R.","Vote, J.","Warren, P.","Thomas, M.","Tyler, I.","Mauger, A.","Close, D.","Jones, M.","Abrams, M.","Cudahy, T.","Caccetta, M.","Lau, I.","Rodger, A.","Laukamp, C.","Ong, C.","Chia, J.","Collings, S.","Rankine, T.","Fraser, R.","Woodcock, R.","Vote, J.","Warren, P.","Thomas, M.","Tyler, I.","Mauger, A.","Close, D.","Jones, M.","Abrams, M."],"onlineResources":[{"url":"https://gsky.nci.org.au/ows/aster?service=WMS&version=1.1.1&request=GetCapabilities","type":"WMS","name":"MgOH_Group_Composition","description":"NCI GSKY Web Map Service (WMS)","version":"1.1.1","applicationProfile":"","protocolRequest":""},{"url":"https://gsky.nci.org.au/ows/aster?service=WCS&version=1.0.0&request=GetCapabilities","type":"WCS","name":"MgOH_Group_Composition","description":"NCI GSKY Web Coverage Service (WCS)","version":"","applicationProfile":"","protocolRequest":""},{"url":"https://thredds.nci.org.au/thredds/dodsC/wx7/aster/vnir/Tasmania/Tas_MgOH_group_composition_reprojected.nc4.html","type":"Unsupported","name":"MgOH_group_composition","description":"NCI OPeNDAP landing page - Tasmania","version":"","applicationProfile":"","protocolRequest":""},{"url":"https://thredds.nci.org.au/thredds/ncss/grid/wx7/aster/vnir/Tasmania/Tas_MgOH_group_composition_reprojected.nc4/dataset.html","type":"WWW","name":"MgOH_group_composition","description":"NCI NetCDF Subset Service - Tasmania","version":"","applicationProfile":"","protocolRequest":""},{"url":"https://thredds.nci.org.au/thredds/fileServer/wx7/aster/vnir/Tasmania/Tas_MgOH_group_composition_reprojected.nc4","type":"WWW","name":"MgOH_group_composition","description":"NCI NetCDF file download via HTTP - Tasmania","version":"","applicationProfile":"","protocolRequest":""},{"url":"https://doi.org/10.4225/08/51400D6F7B335","type":"WWW","name":"CSIRO Data Access Portal Record","description":"","version":"","applicationProfile":"","protocolRequest":""}],"geographicElements":[{"type":"bbox","eastBoundLongitude":155.0,"westBoundLongitude":111.5,"northBoundLatitude":-9.0,"southBoundLatitude":-44.5}],"descriptiveKeywords":["Earth Sciences",""],"datasetURIs":["10.25914/5f224f1141027"],"constraints":["https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","RestrictionCode: restricted","Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International","RestrictionCode: license"],"useLimitConstraints":["Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International","RestrictionCode: license"],"accessConstraints":["RestrictionCode: restricted"],"childRecords":[],"date":"2018-04-10T00:00:00 UTC","minScale":null,"maxScale":null,"knownLayerIds":["aster-mgoh-group-comp"],"knownLayerNames":["MgOH group composition"],"knownLayerDescriptions":["1. Band ratio: B7/B8Blue-cyan is magnesite-dolomite, amphibole, chlorite\tRed is calcite, epidote, amphibole"]}],"relatedRecords":[],"capabilityRecords":[]},{"name":"AlOH group content","hidden":false,"description":"1. Band ratio: (B5+B7)/B6Blue is low abundance, Red is high abundance potentially includes: phengite, muscovite, paragonite, lepidolite, illite, brammalite, montmorillonite, beidellite, kaolinite, dickite","id":"aster-aloh-group-content","proxyUrl":null,"proxyGetFeatureInfoUrl":null,"proxyCountUrl":null,"proxyStyleUrl":null,"proxyDownloadUrl":null,"mapStyles":null,"feature_count":0,"singleTile":false,"legendImg":null,"previewImg":null,"group":"ASTER Mineral Maps","layerMode":"NA","cswRecords":[{"name":"National ASTER Map AlOH group content","resourceProvider":"Resources Division","id":"f1168_3523_3375_4697","recordInfoUrl":"https://geonetwork.nci.org.au/geonetwork/srv/eng/catalog.search#/metadata/f1168_3523_3375_4697","description":"1. Band ratio: (B5+B7)/B6 Blue is low abundance, Red is high abundance potentially includes: phengite, muscovite, paragonite, lepidolite, illite, brammalite, montmorillonite, beidellite, kaolinite, dickite\r\nUseful for mapping: (1) exposed saprolite/saprock (2) clay-rich stratigraphic horizons; (3) lithology-overprinting hydrothermal phyllic (e.g. white mica) alteration; and (4) clay-rich diluents in ore systems (e.g. clay in iron ore). Also combine with AlOH composition to help map: (1) exposed in situ parent material persisting through \"cover\" which can be expressed as: (a) more abundant AlOH content + (b) long-wavelength (warmer colour) AlOH composition (e.g. muscovite/phengite).\n\n\n--\nThis record represents data published by NCI. It uses catalogue metadata modified from Geoscience Australia. See our Record Lineage Information for more details.","noCache":false,"service":false,"adminArea":null,"contactOrg":"Commonwealth Scientific & Industrial Research Organisation (CSIRO)","contactPerson":"Cudahy, T.","funderOrg":"Unknown","authors":["Cudahy, T.","Caccetta, M.","Lau, I.","Rodger, A.","Laukamp, C.","Ong, C.","Chia, J.","Collings, S.","Rankine, T.","Fraser, R.","Woodcock, R.","Vote, J.","Warren, P.","Thomas, M.","Tyler, I.","Mauger, A.","Close, D.","Jones, M.","Abrams, M.","Cud