7772, and; the same seven-class interval binning and colour scheme applied to the source point data in the Deformation/Metamorphism/Alteration Age Data layer (classification 2).","id":"geochron_metamorphic_age_grid","proxyUrl":null,"proxyGetFeatureInfoUrl":null,"proxyCountUrl":null,"proxyStyleUrl":null,"proxyDownloadUrl":null,"mapStyles":null,"feature_count":0,"singleTile":false,"legendImg":null,"previewImg":null,"group":"Geochronology","layerMode":"NA","cswRecords":[{"name":"Deformation/Metamorphism/Alteration Age Grid","resourceProvider":"Unknown","id":"e9321d6b493269b4bf6fda5cfed881fcaeb28c8c","recordInfoUrl":"https://portal.auscope.org.au/geonetwork/srv/eng/catalog.search#/metadata/e9321d6b493269b4bf6fda5cfed881fcaeb28c8c","description":"This grid is an interpolation of deformation/metamorphism/alteration age point data held in the Isotopic Atlas as of February 2021.  Data added to the Isotopic Atlas after February 2021 is not represented in this grid. The grid was generated with Esri's ArcMap Spatial Analyst interpolation tool using the Natural Neighbor algorithm and 0.01 degree cell size.  Two classifications are provided for this grid; a Jenks natural breaks classification with ten classes (classification 1) as per Champion (2013) http://pid.geoscience.gov.au/dataset/ga/77772, and; the same seven-class interval binning and colour scheme applied to the source point data in the Deformation/Metamorphism/Alteration Age Data layer (classification 2).","noCache":false,"service":false,"adminArea":null,"contactOrg":"Geoscience Australia","contactPerson":null,"funderOrg":"Unknown","authors":[],"onlineResources":[{"url":"https://services.ga.gov.au/gis/geochronology-isotopes/ows?SERVICE=WMS&","type":"WMS","name":"isotope:geochron_metamorphic_age_grid","description":"Deformation/Metamorphism/Alteration Age Grid","version":"1.1.1","applicationProfile":"","protocolRequest":""}],"geographicElements":[{"type":"bbox","eastBoundLongitude":151.7542958,"westBoundLongitude":115.3142958,"northBoundLatitude":-11.664544410000001,"southBoundLatitude":-41.21454441}],"descriptiveKeywords":["Isotopes","Geochronology","Isotope Geochemistry","metamorphic age","World","Earth Sciences"],"datasetURIs":[],"constraints":["https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0"],"useLimitConstraints":["https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0"],"accessConstraints":[],"childRecords":[],"date":"2023-08-18T00:00:00 UTC","minScale":null,"maxScale":null,"knownLayerIds":["geochron_metamorphic_age_grid"],"knownLayerNames":["GA Deforma/Metamorph/Alter Age Grid"],"knownLayerDescriptions":["This grid is an interpolation of deformation/metamorphism/alteration age point data held in the Isotopic Atlas as of February 2021. Data added to the Isotopic Atlas after February 2021 is not represented in this grid. The grid was generated with Esri's ArcMap Spatial Analyst interpolation tool using the Natural Neighbor algorithm and 0.01 degree cell size. Two classifications are provided for this grid; a Jenks natural breaks classification with ten classes (classification 1) as per Champion (2013) http://pid.geoscience.gov.au/dataset/ga/77772, and; the same seven-class interval binning and colour scheme applied to the source point data in the Deformation/Metamorphism/Alteration Age Data layer (classification 2)."]}],"relatedRecords":[],"capabilityRecords":[]},{"name":"GA Sedimentary Processes Age Data","hidden":false,"description":"A subset of the All Geochronology layer, comprising summary radiometric age results relating to sedimentary processes, with data derived from both Geoscience Australia (GA) and literature-compiled sources. Each result links to information about the sample, sample collection site, method of analysis, and the source publication information. A large proportion constrain the youngest detrital mineral component in order to provide a maximum estimate for the age of sediment deposition. These rarely reflect the true depositional age of sediments and sedimentary rocks. Full detrital provenance results are not available through this service. Complete analytical data for GA results are available from Geochron Delivery: http://www.ga.gov.au/geochron-sapub-web/.","id":"interpreted_age_samples_sedimentary_processes","proxyUrl":null,"proxyGetFeatureInfoUrl":null,"proxyCountUrl":null,"proxyStyleUrl":null,"proxyDownloadUrl":null,"mapStyles":null,"feature_count":0,"singleTile":false,"legendImg":null,"previewImg":null,"group":"Geochronology","layerMode":"NA","supportsCsvDownloads":true,"cswRecords":[{"name":"Sedimentary Processes Age Data","resourceProvider":"Unknown","id":"9a2cd063f45158dfba05921df7061ebd04f562e0","recordInfoUrl":"https://portal.auscope.org.au/geonetwork/srv/eng/catalog.search#/metadata/9a2cd063f45158dfba05921df7061ebd04f562e0","description":"A subset of the All Geochronology layer, comprising summary radiometric age results relating to sedimentary processes, with data derived from both Geoscience Australia (GA) and literature-compiled sources. Each result links to information about the sample, sample collection site, method of analysis, and the source publication information. A large proportion constrain the youngest detrital mineral component in order to provide a maximum estimate for the age of sediment deposition. These rarely reflect the true depositional age of sediments and sedimentary rocks. Full detrital provenance results are not available through this service. Complete analytical data for GA results are available from Geochron Delivery: http://www.ga.gov.au/geochron-sapub-web/.","noCache":false,"service":false,"adminArea":null,"contactOrg":"Geoscience Australia","contactPerson":null,"funderOrg":"Unknown","authors":[],"onlineResources":[{"url":"https://services.ga.gov.au/gis/geochronology-isotopes/wfs","type":"WFS","name":"isotope:interpreted_age_samples_sedimentary_processes","description":"Sedimentary Processes Age Data","version":"","applicationProfile":"","protocolRequest":""},{"url":"https://services.ga.gov.au/gis/geochronology-isotopes/ows?SERVICE=WMS&","type":"WMS","name":"isotope:interpreted_age_samples_sedimentary_processes","description":"Sedimentary Processes Age Data","version":"1.1.1","applicationProfile":"","protocolRequest":""}],"geographicElements":[{"type":"bbox","eastBoundLongitude":158.0,"westBoundLongitude":45.0,"northBoundLatitude":-2.0,"southBoundLatitude":-76.0}],"descriptiveKeywords":["detrital","geochronology","Earth Sciences","isotopic age","U-Pb dating","isotope","radiometric dating","World","sediments"],"datasetURIs":[],"constraints":["","https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0"],"useLimitConstraints":["https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0"],"accessConstraints":[],"childRecords":[],"date":"2023-08-17T14:00:00 UTC","minScale":null,"maxScale":null,"knownLayerIds":["interpreted_age_samples_sedimentary_processes"],"knownLayerNames":["GA Sedimentary Processes Age Data"],"knownLayerDescriptions":["A subset of the All Geochronology layer, comprising summary radiometric age results relating to sedimentary processes, with data derived from both Geoscience Australia (GA) and literature-compiled sources. Each result links to information about the sample, sample collection site, method of analysis, and the source publication information. A large proportion constrain the youngest detrital mineral component in order to provide a maximum estimate for the age of sediment deposition. These rarely reflect the true depositional age of sediments and sedimentary rocks. Full detrital provenance results are not available through this service. Complete analytical data for GA results are available from Geochron Delivery: http://www.ga.gov.au/geochron-sapub-web/."]},{"name":"Sedimentary Processes Age Data","resourceProvider":"Unknown","id":"5fdc3bc729c534e1c4491eb61941f5ff7082d0fc","recordInfoUrl":"https://portal.auscope.org.au/geonetwork/srv/eng/catalog.search#/metadata/5fdc3bc729c534e1c4491eb61941f5ff7082d0fc","description":"A subset of the All Geochronology layer, comprising summary radiometric age results relating to sedimentary processes, with data derived from both Geoscience Australia (GA) and literature-compiled sources. Each result links to information about the sample, sample collection site, method of analysis, and the source publication information. A large proportion constrain the youngest detrital mineral component in order to provide a maximum estimate for the age of sediment deposition. These rarely reflect the true depositional age of sediments and sedimentary rocks. Full detrital provenance results are not available through this service. Complete analytical data for GA results are available from Geochron Delivery: http://www.ga.gov.au/geochron-sapub-web/.","noCache":false,"service":false,"adminArea":null,"contactOrg":"Geoscience Australia","contactPerson":null,"funderOrg":"Unknown","authors":[],"onlineResources":[{"url":"https://services.ga.gov.au/gis/geochronology-isotopes/wfs","type":"WFS","name":"isotope:interpreted_age_samples_sedimentary_processes","description":"Sedimentary Processes Age Data","version":"","applicationProfile":"","protocolRequest":""},{"url":"https://services.ga.gov.au/gis/geochronology-isotopes/ows?SERVICE=WMS&","type":"WMS","name":"isotope:interpreted_age_samples_sedimentary_processes","description":"Sedimentary Processes Age Data","version":"1.1.1","applicationProfile":"","protocolRequest":""}],"geographicElements":[{"type":"bbox","eastBoundLongitude":158.0,"westBoundLongitude":45.0,"northBoundLatitude":-2.0,"southBoundLatitude":-76.0}],"descriptiveKeywords":["detrital","geochronology","Earth Sciences","isotopic age","U-Pb dating","isotope","radiometric dating","World","sediments"],"datasetURIs":[],"constraints":["","https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0"],"useLimitConstraints":["https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0"],"accessConstraints":[],"childRecords":[],"date":"2023-08-18T00:00:00 UTC","minScale":null,"maxScale":null,"knownLayerIds":["interpreted_age_samples_sedimentary_processes"],"knownLayerNames":["GA Sedimentary Processes Age Data"],"knownLayerDescriptions":["A subset of the All Geochronology layer, comprising summary radiometric age results relating to sedimentary processes, with data derived from both Geoscience Australia (GA) and literature-compiled sources. Each result links to information about the sample, sample collection site, method of analysis, and the source publication information. A large proportion constrain the youngest detrital mineral component in order to provide a maximum estimate for the age of sediment deposition. These rarely reflect the true depositional age of sediments and sedimentary rocks. Full detrital provenance results are not available through this service. Complete analytical data for GA results are available from Geochron Delivery: http://www.ga.gov.au/geochron-sapub-web/."]}],"relatedRecords":[],"capabilityRecords":[]},{"name":"GA Maximum Depositional Age Grid","hidden":false,"description":"This grid is an interpolation of maximum depositional age point data held in the Isotopic Atlas as of February 2021. Data added to the Isotopic Atlas after February 2021 is not represented in this grid. The grid was generated with Esri's ArcMap Spatial Analyst interpolation tool using the Natural Neighbor algorithm and 0.01 degree cell size. Two classifications are provided for this grid; a Jenks natural breaks classification with ten classes (classification 1) as per Champion (2013) http://pid.geoscience.gov.au/dataset/ga/77772, and; the same seven-class interval binning and colour scheme applied to the source point data in the Sedimentary Processes Age Data layer (classification 2).","id":"geochron_maxdep_age_grid","proxyUrl":null,"proxyGetFeatureInfoUrl":null,"proxyCountUrl":null,"proxyStyleUrl":null,"proxyDownloadUrl":null,"mapStyles":null,"feature_count":0,"singleTile":false,"legendImg":null,"previewImg":null,"group":"Geochronology","layerMode":"NA","cswRecords":[{"name":"Maximum Depositional Age Grid","resourceProvider":"Unknown","id":"bf7f74cd219f497174a552284223aeb5a8ef3f40","recordInfoUrl":"https://portal.auscope.org.au/geonetwork/srv/eng/catalog.search#/metadata/bf7f74cd219f497174a552284223aeb5a8ef3f40","description":"This grid is an interpolation of maximum depositional age point data held in the Isotopic Atlas as of February 2021.  Data added to the Isotopic Atlas after February 2021 is not represented in this grid. The grid was generated with Esri's ArcMap Spatial Analyst interpolation tool using the Natural Neighbor algorithm and 0.01 degree cell size.  Two classifications are provided for this grid; a Jenks natural breaks classification with ten classes (classification 1) as per Champion (2013) http://pid.geoscience.gov.au/dataset/ga/77772, and; the same seven-class interval binning and colour scheme applied to the source point data in the Sedimentary Processes Age Data layer (classification 2).","noCache":false,"service":false,"adminArea":null,"contactOrg":"Geoscience Australia","contactPerson":null,"funderOrg":"Unknown","authors":[],"onlineResources":[{"url":"https://services.ga.gov.au/gis/geochronology-isotopes/ows?SERVICE=WMS&","type":"WMS","name":"isotope:geochron_maxdep_age_grid","description":"Maximum Depositional Age Grid","version":"1.1.1","applicationProfile":"","protocolRequest":""}],"geographicElements":[{"type":"bbox","eastBoundLongitude":151.7539858,"westBoundLongitude":113.6039858,"northBoundLatitude":-12.086469429999998,"southBoundLatitude":-41.63646943}],"descriptiveKeywords":["Isotopes","Geochronology","Isotope Geochemistry","maximum depositional age","World","Earth Sciences"],"datasetURIs":[],"constraints":["https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0"],"useLimitConstraints":["https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0"],"accessConstraints":[],"childRecords":[],"date":"2023-08-18T00:00:00 UTC","minScale":null,"maxScale":null,"knownLayerIds":["geochron_maxdep_age_grid"],"knownLayerNames":["GA Maximum Depositional Age Grid"],"knownLayerDescriptions":["This grid is an interpolation of maximum depositional age point data held in the Isotopic Atlas as of February 2021. Data added to the Isotopic Atlas after February 2021 is not represented in this grid. The grid was generated with Esri's ArcMap Spatial Analyst interpolation tool using the Natural Neighbor algorithm and 0.01 degree cell size. Two classifications are provided for this grid; a Jenks natural breaks classification with ten classes (classification 1) as per Champion (2013) http://pid.geoscience.gov.au/dataset/ga/77772, and; the same seven-class interval binning and colour scheme applied to the source point data in the Sedimentary Processes Age Data layer (classification 2)."]}],"relatedRecords":[],"capabilityRecords":[]},{"name":"GA Sm-Nd Isotope Data","hidden":false,"description":"A compilation of full analytical data tables for publicly-available Sm-Nd isotope data from Geoscience Australia (GA), State and Geological Surveys, and from literature-compiled sources. Each result links to information about the sample (including unit name, lithology and age), sample collection site, method of analysis, analytical errors, associated Reference Standards and analytical values, and references for location, age data, and the source publication information. Refer to Champion (2013) for further details: http://pid.geoscience.gov.au/dataset/ga/77772. Note that intervals used for the T2DM, Residence Age and Crystallisation Age are rounded to the nearest 100 Ma.","id":"isotopes_smnd","proxyUrl":null,"proxyGetFeatureInfoUrl":null,"proxyCountUrl":null,"proxyStyleUrl":null,"proxyDownloadUrl":null,"mapStyles":null,"feature_count":0,"singleTile":false,"legendImg":null,"previewImg":null,"group":"Isotopes","layerMode":"NA","supportsCsvDownloads":true,"cswRecords":[{"name":"Sm-Nd Isotope Data","resourceProvider":"Unknown","id":"062775c92ea97855389a6658d6548f38de45906e","recordInfoUrl":"https://portal.auscope.org.au/geonetwork/srv/eng/catalog.search#/metadata/062775c92ea97855389a6658d6548f38de45906e","description":"A compilation of full analytical data tables for publicly-available Sm-Nd isotope data from Geoscience Australia (GA), State and Geological Surveys, and from literature-compiled sources. Each result links to information about the sample (including unit name, lithology and age), sample collection site, method of analysis, analytical errors, associated Reference Standards and analytical values, and references for location, age data, and the source publication information. Refer to Champion (2013) for further details: http://pid.geoscience.gov.au/dataset/ga/77772.\nNote that intervals used for the T2DM, Residence Age and Crystallisation Age are rounded to the nearest 100 Ma.","noCache":false,"service":false,"adminArea":null,"contactOrg":"Geoscience Australia","contactPerson":null,"funderOrg":"Unknown","authors":[],"onlineResources":[{"url":"https://services.ga.gov.au/gis/geochronology-isotopes/wfs","type":"WFS","name":"isotope:isotopes_smnd","description":"Sm-Nd Isotope Data","version":"","applicationProfile":"","protocolRequest":""},{"url":"https://services.ga.gov.au/gis/geochronology-isotopes/ows?SERVICE=WMS&","type":"WMS","name":"isotope:isotopes_smnd","description":"Sm-Nd Isotope Data","version":"1.1.1","applicationProfile":"","protocolRequest":""}],"geographicElements":[{"type":"bbox","eastBoundLongitude":155.0,"westBoundLongitude":112.0,"northBoundLatitude":-9.0,"southBoundLatitude":-45.0}],"descriptiveKeywords":["Earth Sciences","Sm-Nd isotopes","epsilon Nd","model age","isotope geochemistry","radiogenic isotopes","World","Isotopes"],"datasetURIs":[],"constraints":["","https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0"],"useLimitConstraints":["https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0"],"accessConstraints":[],"childRecords":[],"date":"2023-08-18T00:00:00 UTC","minScale":null,"maxScale":null,"knownLayerIds":["isotopes_smnd"],"knownLayerNames":["GA Sm-Nd Isotope Data"],"knownLayerDescriptions":["A compilation of full analytical data tables for publicly-available Sm-Nd isotope data from Geoscience Australia (GA), State and Geological Surveys, and from literature-compiled sources. Each result links to information about the sample (including unit name, lithology and age), sample collection site, method of analysis, analytical errors, associated Reference Standards and analytical values, and references for location, age data, and the source publication information. Refer to Champion (2013) for further details: http://pid.geoscience.gov.au/dataset/ga/77772. Note that intervals used for the T2DM, Residence Age and Crystallisation Age are rounded to the nearest 100 Ma."]}],"relatedRecords":[],"capabilityRecords":[]},{"name":"GA Sm-Nd Model Age (T2DM) Grid","hidden":false,"description":"This is an interpolated grid of Nd two-stage model ages, based on whole-rock Nd isotopic analyses from felsic magmatic rocks, particularly focusing on I- and A-type granites and volcanic rocks. The data provides an estimate of the timing of extraction from the mantle of the middle to lower crustal source regions from which the felsic melts were generated. The point data used for the interpolation is the “felsic igneous rock” subset of the Sm-Nd data held in the Isotopic Atlas as of February 2021. Point data added to the Isotopic Atlas after February 2021 is not represented in this grid. The grid was generated with Esri's ArcMap Spatial Analyst interpolation tool using the Natural Neighbor algorithm and 0.01 degree cell size. Two classifications are provided for this grid; a Jenks natural breaks classification with ten classes (classification 1) as per Champion (2013) http://pid.geoscience.gov.au/dataset/ga/77772, and; the same nine-class interval binning and colour scheme applied to the source point data in the Sm-Nd Isotope Data layer (classification 2).","id":"smnd_t2dm_grid","proxyUrl":null,"proxyGetFeatureInfoUrl":null,"proxyCountUrl":null,"proxyStyleUrl":null,"proxyDownloadUrl":null,"mapStyles":null,"feature_count":0,"singleTile":false,"legendImg":null,"previewImg":null,"group":"Isotopes","layerMode":"NA","cswRecords":[{"name":"Sm-Nd Model Age (T2DM) Grid (felsic igneous rocks)","resourceProvider":"Unknown","id":"b2b6458693f070a55d631bba59b3413853780b0c","recordInfoUrl":"https://portal.auscope.org.au/geonetwork/srv/eng/catalog.search#/metadata/b2b6458693f070a55d631bba59b3413853780b0c","description":"This is an interpolated grid of Nd two-stage model ages, based on whole-rock Nd isotopic analyses from felsic magmatic rocks, particularly focusing on I- and A-type granites and volcanic rocks. The data provides an estimate of the timing of extraction from the mantle of the middle to lower crustal source regions from which the felsic melts were generated. The point data used for the interpolation is the “felsic igneous rock” subset of the Sm-Nd data held in the Isotopic Atlas as of February 2021.  Point data added to the Isotopic Atlas after February 2021 is not represented in this grid.  The grid was generated with Esri's ArcMap Spatial Analyst interpolation tool using the Natural Neighbor algorithm and 0.01 degree cell size.  Two classifications are provided for this grid; a Jenks natural breaks classification with ten classes (classification 1) as per Champion (2013) http://pid.geoscience.gov.au/dataset/ga/77772, and; the same nine-class interval binning and colour scheme applied to the source point data in the Sm-Nd Isotope Data layer (classification 2).","noCache":false,"service":false,"adminArea":null,"contactOrg":"Geoscience Australia","contactPerson":null,"funderOrg":"Unknown","authors":[],"onlineResources":[{"url":"https://services.ga.gov.au/gis/geochronology-isotopes/ows?SERVICE=WMS&","type":"WMS","name":"isotope:smnd_t2dm_grid","description":"Sm-Nd Model Age (T2DM) Grid (felsic igneous rocks)","version":"1.1.1","applicationProfile":"","protocolRequest":""}],"geographicElements":[{"type":"bbox","eastBoundLongitude":152.94782980000002,"westBoundLongitude":114.7478298,"northBoundLatitude":-11.624332920000004,"southBoundLatitude":-43.494332920000005}],"descriptiveKeywords":["Isotopes","Geochronology","Isotope Geochemistry","Sm-Nd","T2DM","model age","World","Earth Sciences"],"datasetURIs":[],"constraints":["https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0"],"useLimitConstraints":["https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0"],"accessConstraints":[],"childRecords":[],"date":"2023-08-18T00:00:00 UTC","minScale":null,"maxScale":null,"knownLayerIds":["smnd_t2dm_grid"],"knownLayerNames":["GA Sm-Nd Model Age (T2DM) Grid"],"knownLayerDescriptions":["This is an interpolated grid of Nd two-stage model ages, based on whole-rock Nd isotopic analyses from felsic magmatic rocks, particularly focusing on I- and A-type granites and volcanic rocks. The data provides an estimate of the timing of extraction from the mantle of the middle to lower crustal source regions from which the felsic melts were generated. The point data used for the interpolation is the “felsic igneous rock” subset of the Sm-Nd data held in the Isotopic Atlas as of February 2021. Point data added to the Isotopic Atlas after February 2021 is not represented in this grid. The grid was generated with Esri's ArcMap Spatial Analyst interpolation tool using the Natural Neighbor algorithm and 0.01 degree cell size. Two classifications are provided for this grid; a Jenks natural breaks classification with ten classes (classification 1) as per Champion (2013) http://pid.geoscience.gov.au/dataset/ga/77772, and; the same nine-class interval binning and colour scheme applied to the source point data in the Sm-Nd Isotope Data layer (classification 2)."]}],"relatedRecords":[],"capabilityRecords":[]},{"name":"GA Sm-Nd Epsilon Grid","hidden":false,"description":"This is an interpolated grid of Sm-Nd epsilon values, based on whole-rock Nd isotopic analyses from felsic magmatic rocks, particularly focusing on I- and A-type granites and volcanic rocks. The point data used for the interpolation is the “felsic igneous rock” subset of the Sm-Nd data held in the Isotopic Atlas as of February 2021. Point data added to the Isotopic Atlas after February 2021 is not represented in this grid. The grid was generated with Esri's ArcMap Spatial Analyst interpolation tool using the Natural Neighbor algorithm and 0.01 degree cell size. Two classifications are provided for this grid; a Jenks natural breaks classification with ten classes (classification 1) as per Champion (2013) http://pid.geoscience.gov.au/dataset/ga/77772, and; the same seven-class interval binning and colour scheme applied to the source point data in the Sm-Nd Isotope Data layer (classification 2).","id":"smnd_epsilon_grid","proxyUrl":null,"proxyGetFeatureInfoUrl":null,"proxyCountUrl":null,"proxyStyleUrl":null,"proxyDownloadUrl":null,"mapStyles":null,"feature_count":0,"singleTile":false,"legendImg":null,"previewImg":null,"group":"Isotopes","layerMode":"NA","cswRecords":[{"name":"Sm-Nd Epsilon Grid (felsic igneous rocks)","resourceProvider":"Unknown","id":"9a743a71e7680b323e30c1e5721d9732c9741476","recordInfoUrl":"https://portal.auscope.org.au/geonetwork/srv/eng/catalog.search#/metadata/9a743a71e7680b323e30c1e5721d9732c9741476","description":"This is an interpolated grid of Sm-Nd epsilon values, based on whole-rock Nd isotopic analyses from felsic magmatic rocks, particularly focusing on I- and A-type granites and volcanic rocks.  The point data used for the interpolation is the “felsic igneous rock” subset of the Sm-Nd data held in the Isotopic Atlas as of February 2021.  Point data added to the Isotopic Atlas after February 2021 is not represented in this grid.  The grid was generated with Esri's ArcMap Spatial Analyst interpolation tool using the Natural Neighbor algorithm and 0.01 degree cell size.  Two classifications are provided for this grid; a Jenks natural breaks classification with ten classes (classification 1) as per Champion (2013) http://pid.geoscience.gov.au/dataset/ga/77772, and; the same seven-class interval binning and colour scheme applied to the source point data in the Sm-Nd Isotope Data layer (classification 2).","noCache":false,"service":false,"adminArea":null,"contactOrg":"Geoscience Australia","contactPerson":null,"funderOrg":"Unknown","authors":[],"onlineResources":[{"url":"https://services.ga.gov.au/gis/geochronology-isotopes/ows?SERVICE=WMS&","type":"WMS","name":"isotope:smnd_epsilon_grid","description":"Sm-Nd Epsilon Grid (felsic igneous rocks)","version":"1.1.1","applicationProfile":"","protocolRequest":""}],"geographicElements":[{"type":"bbox","eastBoundLongitude":152.94782980000002,"westBoundLongitude":114.7478298,"northBoundLatitude":-11.624332920000004,"southBoundLatitude":-43.494332920000005},{"type":"bbox","eastBoundLongitude":152.94782980000002,"westBoundLongitude":114.7478298,"northBoundLatitude":-11.624332920000004,"southBoundLatitude":-43.494332920000005}],"descriptiveKeywords":["epsilon","Earth Science","Geochronology","Earth Sciences","Isotope Geochemistry","Sm-Nd","World","Isotopes"],"datasetURIs":[],"constraints":["","© Commonwealth of Australia (Geoscience Australia) 2021. This product is released under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International Licence","https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0"],"useLimitConstraints":["https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0"],"accessConstraints":[],"childRecords":[],"date":"2023-08-18T00:00:00 UTC","minScale":null,"maxScale":null,"knownLayerIds":["smnd_epsilon_grid"],"knownLayerNames":["GA Sm-Nd Epsilon Grid"],"knownLayerDescriptions":["This is an interpolated grid of Sm-Nd epsilon values, based on whole-rock Nd isotopic analyses from felsic magmatic rocks, particularly focusing on I- and A-type granites and volcanic rocks. The point data used for the interpolation is the “felsic igneous rock” subset of the Sm-Nd data held in the Isotopic Atlas as of February 2021. Point data added to the Isotopic Atlas after February 2021 is not represented in this grid. The grid was generated with Esri's ArcMap Spatial Analyst interpolation tool using the Natural Neighbor algorithm and 0.01 degree cell size. Two classifications are provided for this grid; a Jenks natural breaks classification with ten classes (classification 1) as per Champion (2013) http://pid.geoscience.gov.au/dataset/ga/77772, and; the same seven-class interval binning and colour scheme applied to the source point data in the Sm-Nd Isotope Data layer (classification 2)."]}],"relatedRecords":[],"capabilityRecords":[]},{"name":"GA Sm-Nd Residence Time Grid","hidden":false,"description":"This is an interpolated grid of Nd residence time values, based on whole-rock Nd isotopic analyses from felsic magmatic rocks, particularly focusing on I- and A-type granites and volcanic rocks. The data provides an estimate of the duration for material residing in the crust prior to its last melting event. The point data used for the interpolation is the “felsic igneous rock” subset of the Sm-Nd data held in the Isotopic Atlas as of February 2021. Point data added to the Isotopic Atlas after February 2021 is not represented in this grid. The grid was generated with Esri's ArcMap Spatial Analyst interpolation tool using the Natural Neighbor algorithm and 0.01 degree cell size. Two classifications are provided for this grid; a Jenks natural breaks classification with ten classes (classification 1) as per Champion (2013) http://pid.geoscience.gov.au/dataset/ga/77772, and; the same nine-class interval binning and colour scheme applied to the source point data in the Sm-Nd Isotope Data layer (classification 2).","id":"smnd_residence_time_grid","proxyUrl":null,"proxyGetFeatureInfoUrl":null,"proxyCountUrl":null,"proxyStyleUrl":null,"proxyDownloadUrl":null,"mapStyles":null,"feature_count":0,"singleTile":false,"legendImg":null,"previewImg":null,"group":"Isotopes","layerMode":"NA","cswRecords":[{"name":"Sm-Nd Residence Time Grid (felsic igneous rocks)","resourceProvider":"Unknown","id":"a43d3f1708394bb5dff9619b2e213ab538605c89","recordInfoUrl":"https://portal.auscope.org.au/geonetwork/srv/eng/catalog.search#/metadata/a43d3f1708394bb5dff9619b2e213ab538605c89","description":"This is an interpolated grid of Nd residence time values, based on whole-rock Nd isotopic analyses from felsic magmatic rocks, particularly focusing on I- and A-type granites and volcanic rocks.  The data provides an estimate of the duration for material residing in the crust prior to its last melting event. The point data used for the interpolation is the “felsic igneous rock” subset of the Sm-Nd data held in the Isotopic Atlas as of February 2021.  Point data added to the Isotopic Atlas after February 2021 is not represented in this grid.  The grid was generated with Esri's ArcMap Spatial Analyst interpolation tool using the Natural Neighbor algorithm and 0.01 degree cell size.  Two classifications are provided for this grid; a Jenks natural breaks classification with ten classes (classification 1) as per Champion (2013) http://pid.geoscience.gov.au/dataset/ga/77772, and; the same nine-class interval binning and colour scheme applied to the source point data in the Sm-Nd Isotope Data layer (classification 2).","noCache":false,"service":false,"adminArea":null,"contactOrg":"Geoscience Australia","contactPerson":null,"funderOrg":"Unknown","authors":[],"onlineResources":[{"url":"https://services.ga.gov.au/gis/geochronology-isotopes/ows?SERVICE=WMS&","type":"WMS","name":"isotope:smnd_residence_time_grid","description":"Sm-Nd Residence Time Grid (felsic igneous rocks)","version":"1.1.1","applicationProfile":"","protocolRequest":""}],"geographicElements":[{"type":"bbox","eastBoundLongitude":152.94782980000002,"westBoundLongitude":114.7478298,"northBoundLatitude":-11.624332920000004,"southBoundLatitude":-43.494332920000005}],"descriptiveKeywords":["Isotopes","Geochronology","Isotope Geochemistry","Sm-Nd","residence time","World","Earth Sciences"],"datasetURIs":[],"constraints":["https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0"],"useLimitConstraints":["https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0"],"accessConstraints":[],"childRecords":[],"date":"2023-08-18T00:00:00 UTC","minScale":null,"maxScale":null,"knownLayerIds":["smnd_residence_time_grid"],"knownLayerNames":["GA Sm-Nd Residence Time Grid"],"knownLayerDescriptions":["This is an interpolated grid of Nd residence time values, based on whole-rock Nd isotopic analyses from felsic magmatic rocks, particularly focusing on I- and A-type granites and volcanic rocks. The data provides an estimate of the duration for material residing in the crust prior to its last melting event. The point data used for the interpolation is the “felsic igneous rock” subset of the Sm-Nd data held in the Isotopic Atlas as of February 2021. Point data added to the Isotopic Atlas after February 2021 is not represented in this grid. The grid was generated with Esri's ArcMap Spatial Analyst interpolation tool using the Natural Neighbor algorithm and 0.01 degree cell size. Two classifications are provided for this grid; a Jenks natural breaks classification with ten classes (classification 1) as per Champion (2013) http://pid.geoscience.gov.au/dataset/ga/77772, and; the same nine-class interval binning and colour scheme applied to the source point data in the Sm-Nd Isotope Data layer (classification 2)."]}],"relatedRecords":[],"capabilityRecords":[]},{"name":"GA Lu-Hf Isotopes: Summary Data","hidden":false,"description":"A compilation of summary information for publicly-available Lu-Hf isotope and associated O-isotope data from both Geoscience Australia (GA) and literature-compiled sources. Each result links to information about the sample, sample collection site, method of analysis, and the source publication information. Full analytical data tables are available through the complementary service. Refer to Waltenberg et al (2021) for further details: http://dx.doi.org/10.11636/Record.2021.016.","id":"isotopes_hf","proxyUrl":null,"proxyGetFeatureInfoUrl":null,"proxyCountUrl":null,"proxyStyleUrl":null,"proxyDownloadUrl":null,"mapStyles":null,"feature_count":0,"singleTile":false,"legendImg":null,"previewImg":null,"group":"Isotopes","layerMode":"NA","supportsCsvDownloads":true,"cswRecords":[{"name":"Lu-Hf Isotopes - Summary Data","resourceProvider":"Unknown","id":"57c273216ee7644a77d4bc558f67dda0869ddf60","recordInfoUrl":"https://portal.auscope.org.au/geonetwork/srv/eng/catalog.search#/metadata/57c273216ee7644a77d4bc558f67dda0869ddf60","description":"A compilation of summary information for publicly-available Lu-Hf isotope and associated O-isotope data from both Geoscience Australia (GA) and literature-compiled sources. Each result links to information about the sample, sample collection site, method of analysis, and the source publication information. Full analytical data tables are available through the complementary service. Refer to Waltenberg et al (2021) for further details: http://dx.doi.org/10.11636/Record.2021.016.","noCache":false,"service":false,"adminArea":null,"contactOrg":"Geoscience Australia","contactPerson":null,"funderOrg":"Unknown","authors":[],"onlineResources":[{"url":"https://services.ga.gov.au/gis/geochronology-isotopes/wfs","type":"WFS","name":"isotope:isotopes_hf","description":"Lu-Hf Isotopes - Summary Data","version":"","applicationProfile":"","protocolRequest":""},{"url":"https://services.ga.gov.au/gis/geochronology-isotopes/ows?SERVICE=WMS&","type":"WMS","name":"isotope:isotopes_hf","description":"Lu-Hf Isotopes - Summary Data","version":"1.1.1","applicationProfile":"","protocolRequest":""}],"geographicElements":[{"type":"bbox","eastBoundLongitude":155.0,"westBoundLongitude":112.0,"northBoundLatitude":-9.0,"southBoundLatitude":-45.0}],"descriptiveKeywords":["Earth Sciences","Lu-Hf isotopes","model age","isotope geochemistry","radiogenic isotopes","World","Isotopes","epsilon Hf","oxygen isotopes"],"datasetURIs":[],"constraints":["","https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0"],"useLimitConstraints":["https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0"],"accessConstraints":[],"childRecords":[],"date":"2023-08-18T00:00:00 UTC","minScale":null,"maxScale":null,"knownLayerIds":["isotopes_hf"],"knownLayerNames":["GA Lu-Hf Isotopes: Summary Data"],"knownLayerDescriptions":["A compilation of summary information for publicly-available Lu-Hf isotope and associated O-isotope data from both Geoscience Australia (GA) and literature-compiled sources. Each result links to information about the sample, sample collection site, method of analysis, and the source publication information. Full analytical data tables are available through the complementary service. Refer to Waltenberg et al (2021) for further details: http://dx.doi.org/10.11636/Record.2021.016."]}],"relatedRecords":[],"capabilityRecords":[]},{"name":"GA Lu-Hf Model Age (T2DM) Grid","hidden":false,"description":"This is an interpolated grid of Lu-Hf two-stage model ages, based on (primarily zircon) Lu-Hf isotopic analyses from igneous rocks. The data provides an estimate of the timing of extraction from the mantle of the middle to lower crustal source regions from which the melts were generated. The point data used for the interpolation is the median magmatic T2DM data of the summary Lu-Hf dataset held in the Isotopic Atlas as of February 2021. Point data added to the Isotopic Atlas after February 2021 is not represented in this grid. The grid was generated with Esri's ArcMap Spatial Analyst interpolation tool using the Natural Neighbor algorithm and 0.01 degree cell size. Two classifications are provided for this grid; a Jenks natural breaks classification with ten classes (classification 1) as per Champion (2013) http://pid.geoscience.gov.au/dataset/ga/77772, and; the same three-class interval binning and colour scheme applied to the source point data in the Lu-Hf Isotopes - Summary Data layer (classification 2).","id":"luhf_t2dm_grid","proxyUrl":null,"proxyGetFeatureInfoUrl":null,"proxyCountUrl":null,"proxyStyleUrl":null,"proxyDownloadUrl":null,"mapStyles":null,"feature_count":0,"singleTile":false,"legendImg":null,"previewImg":null,"group":"Isotopes","layerMode":"NA","cswRecords":[{"name":"Lu-Hf Model Age (T2DM) Grid (igneous)","resourceProvider":"Unknown","id":"c45f9b5f1b1b164c7f9ed90e5473622c8e639ebc","recordInfoUrl":"https://portal.auscope.org.au/geonetwork/srv/eng/catalog.search#/metadata/c45f9b5f1b1b164c7f9ed90e5473622c8e639ebc","description":"This is an interpolated grid of Lu-Hf two-stage model ages, based on (primarily zircon) Lu-Hf isotopic analyses from igneous rocks.  The data provides an estimate of the timing of extraction from the mantle of the middle to lower crustal source regions from which the melts were generated. The point data used for the interpolation is the median magmatic T2DM data of the summary Lu-Hf dataset held in the Isotopic Atlas as of February 2021. Point data added to the Isotopic Atlas after February 2021 is not represented in this grid.  The grid was generated with Esri's ArcMap Spatial Analyst interpolation tool using the Natural Neighbor algorithm and 0.01 degree cell size.  Two classifications are provided for this grid; a Jenks natural breaks classification with ten classes (classification 1) as per Champion (2013) http://pid.geoscience.gov.au/dataset/ga/77772, and; the same three-class interval binning and colour scheme applied to the source point data in the Lu-Hf Isotopes - Summary Data layer (classification 2).","noCache":false,"service":false,"adminArea":null,"contactOrg":"Geoscience Australia","contactPerson":null,"funderOrg":"Unknown","authors":[],"onlineResources":[{"url":"https://services.ga.gov.au/gis/geochronology-isotopes/ows?SERVICE=WMS&","type":"WMS","name":"isotope:luhf_t2dm_grid","description":"Lu-Hf Model Age (T2DM) Grid (igneous)","version":"1.1.1","applicationProfile":"","protocolRequest":""}],"geographicElements":[{"type":"bbox","eastBoundLongitude":139.836727,"westBoundLong