:"GA Pb-Pb Omega Grid","hidden":false,"description":"This is an interpolated grid of Pb-Pb ω (omega, 232Th/204Pb) data from primarily ore-related rocks and minerals. The point data used for the interpolation is from the Pb-Pb dataset held in the Isotopic Atlas as of February 2021. Point data added to the Isotopic Atlas after February 2021 is not represented in this grid. The grid was generated with Esri's ArcMap Spatial Analyst interpolation tool using the Natural Neighbor algorithm and 0.01 degree cell size. Two classifications are provided for this grid; a Jenks natural breaks classification with ten classes (classification 1) as per Champion (2013) http://pid.geoscience.gov.au/dataset/ga/77772, and; the same seven-class interval binning and colour scheme applied to the source point data in the Pb-Pb Isotope Data layer (classification 2).","id":"pbpb_omega_grid","proxyUrl":null,"proxyGetFeatureInfoUrl":null,"proxyCountUrl":null,"proxyStyleUrl":null,"proxyDownloadUrl":null,"mapStyles":null,"feature_count":0,"singleTile":false,"legendImg":null,"previewImg":null,"group":"Isotopes","layerMode":"NA","cswRecords":[{"name":"Pb-Pb Omega Grid (ores)","resourceProvider":"Unknown","id":"1b9da5d283d24112c7a16557e14635f37935064c","recordInfoUrl":"https://portal.auscope.org.au/geonetwork/srv/eng/catalog.search#/metadata/1b9da5d283d24112c7a16557e14635f37935064c","description":"This is an interpolated grid of Pb-Pb ω (omega, 232Th/204Pb) data from primarily ore-related rocks and minerals.  The point data used for the interpolation is from the Pb-Pb dataset held in the Isotopic Atlas as of February 2021.  Point data added to the Isotopic Atlas after February 2021 is not represented in this grid.  The grid was generated with Esri's ArcMap Spatial Analyst interpolation tool using the Natural Neighbor algorithm and 0.01 degree cell size.  Two classifications are provided for this grid; a Jenks natural breaks classification with ten classes (classification 1) as per Champion (2013) http://pid.geoscience.gov.au/dataset/ga/77772, and; the same seven-class interval binning and colour scheme applied to the source point data in the Pb-Pb Isotope Data layer (classification 2).","noCache":false,"service":false,"adminArea":null,"contactOrg":"Geoscience Australia","contactPerson":null,"funderOrg":"Unknown","authors":[],"onlineResources":[{"url":"https://services.ga.gov.au/gis/geochronology-isotopes/ows?SERVICE=WMS&","type":"WMS","name":"isotope:pbpb_omega_grid","description":"Pb-Pb Omega Grid (ores)","version":"1.1.1","applicationProfile":"","protocolRequest":""}],"geographicElements":[{"type":"bbox","eastBoundLongitude":153.4724,"westBoundLongitude":114.6124,"northBoundLatitude":-10.711800000000004,"southBoundLatitude":-43.171800000000005}],"descriptiveKeywords":["Isotopes","Geochronology","Isotope Geochemistry","Pb-Pb","Omega","World","Earth Sciences"],"datasetURIs":[],"constraints":["https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0"],"useLimitConstraints":["https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0"],"accessConstraints":[],"childRecords":[],"date":"2023-08-18T00:00:00 UTC","minScale":null,"maxScale":null,"knownLayerIds":["pbpb_omega_grid"],"knownLayerNames":["GA Pb-Pb Omega Grid"],"knownLayerDescriptions":["This is an interpolated grid of Pb-Pb ω (omega, 232Th/204Pb) data from primarily ore-related rocks and minerals. The point data used for the interpolation is from the Pb-Pb dataset held in the Isotopic Atlas as of February 2021. Point data added to the Isotopic Atlas after February 2021 is not represented in this grid. The grid was generated with Esri's ArcMap Spatial Analyst interpolation tool using the Natural Neighbor algorithm and 0.01 degree cell size. Two classifications are provided for this grid; a Jenks natural breaks classification with ten classes (classification 1) as per Champion (2013) http://pid.geoscience.gov.au/dataset/ga/77772, and; the same seven-class interval binning and colour scheme applied to the source point data in the Pb-Pb Isotope Data layer (classification 2)."]}],"relatedRecords":[],"capabilityRecords":[]},{"name":"GA Pb-Pb Model Age Grid","hidden":false,"description":"This is an interpolated grid of Pb-Pb model age data from primarily ore-related rocks and minerals. The point data used for the interpolation is from the Pb-Pb dataset held in the Isotopic Atlas as of February 2021, and the model ages are calculated using Stacey and Kramers (1975) Pb-evolution model. Point data added to the Isotopic Atlas after February 2021 is not represented in this grid. The grid was generated with Esri's ArcMap Spatial Analyst interpolation tool using the Natural Neighbor algorithm and 0.01 degree cell size. Two classifications are provided for this grid; a Jenks natural breaks classification with ten classes (classification 1) as per Champion (2013) http://pid.geoscience.gov.au/dataset/ga/77772, and; the same six-class interval binning and colour scheme applied to the source point data in the Pb-Pb Isotope Data layer (classification 2).","id":"pbpb_model_age_grid","proxyUrl":null,"proxyGetFeatureInfoUrl":null,"proxyCountUrl":null,"proxyStyleUrl":null,"proxyDownloadUrl":null,"mapStyles":null,"feature_count":0,"singleTile":false,"legendImg":null,"previewImg":null,"group":"Isotopes","layerMode":"NA","cswRecords":[{"name":"Pb-Pb Model Age Grid (ores)","resourceProvider":"Unknown","id":"69a819cf364145e0df4cbf6b977380637822fc5e","recordInfoUrl":"https://portal.auscope.org.au/geonetwork/srv/eng/catalog.search#/metadata/69a819cf364145e0df4cbf6b977380637822fc5e","description":"This is an interpolated grid of Pb-Pb model age data from primarily ore-related rocks and minerals.  The point data used for the interpolation is from the Pb-Pb dataset held in the Isotopic Atlas as of February 2021, and the model ages are calculated using Stacey and Kramers (1975) Pb-evolution model.  Point data added to the Isotopic Atlas after February 2021 is not represented in this grid.  The grid was generated with Esri's ArcMap Spatial Analyst interpolation tool using the Natural Neighbor algorithm and 0.01 degree cell size.  Two classifications are provided for this grid; a Jenks natural breaks classification with ten classes (classification 1) as per Champion (2013) http://pid.geoscience.gov.au/dataset/ga/77772, and; the same six-class interval binning and colour scheme applied to the source point data in the Pb-Pb Isotope Data layer (classification 2).","noCache":false,"service":false,"adminArea":null,"contactOrg":"Geoscience Australia","contactPerson":null,"funderOrg":"Unknown","authors":[],"onlineResources":[{"url":"https://services.ga.gov.au/gis/geochronology-isotopes/ows?SERVICE=WMS&","type":"WMS","name":"isotope:pbpb_model_age_grid","description":"Pb-Pb Model Age Grid (ores)","version":"1.1.1","applicationProfile":"","protocolRequest":""}],"geographicElements":[{"type":"bbox","eastBoundLongitude":153.4724,"westBoundLongitude":114.6124,"northBoundLatitude":-10.711800000000004,"southBoundLatitude":-43.171800000000005}],"descriptiveKeywords":["Isotopes","Geochronology","Isotope Geochemistry","Pb-Pb","model age","World","Earth Sciences"],"datasetURIs":[],"constraints":["https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0"],"useLimitConstraints":["https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0"],"accessConstraints":[],"childRecords":[],"date":"2023-08-18T00:00:00 UTC","minScale":null,"maxScale":null,"knownLayerIds":["pbpb_model_age_grid"],"knownLayerNames":["GA Pb-Pb Model Age Grid"],"knownLayerDescriptions":["This is an interpolated grid of Pb-Pb model age data from primarily ore-related rocks and minerals. The point data used for the interpolation is from the Pb-Pb dataset held in the Isotopic Atlas as of February 2021, and the model ages are calculated using Stacey and Kramers (1975) Pb-evolution model. Point data added to the Isotopic Atlas after February 2021 is not represented in this grid. The grid was generated with Esri's ArcMap Spatial Analyst interpolation tool using the Natural Neighbor algorithm and 0.01 degree cell size. Two classifications are provided for this grid; a Jenks natural breaks classification with ten classes (classification 1) as per Champion (2013) http://pid.geoscience.gov.au/dataset/ga/77772, and; the same six-class interval binning and colour scheme applied to the source point data in the Pb-Pb Isotope Data layer (classification 2)."]}],"relatedRecords":[],"capabilityRecords":[]},{"name":"GA Rb-Sr Isotope Data","hidden":false,"description":"Analytical data tables for publicly-available Sr-isotope data from Geoscience Australia (GA). Each result links to information about the sample, analytical metadata, and the source publication. Refer to de Caritat et al. (2022) for further details: http://pid.geoscience.gov.au/dataset/ga/71912.","id":"isotopes_rbsr","proxyUrl":null,"proxyGetFeatureInfoUrl":null,"proxyCountUrl":null,"proxyStyleUrl":null,"proxyDownloadUrl":null,"mapStyles":null,"feature_count":0,"singleTile":false,"legendImg":null,"previewImg":null,"group":"Isotopes","layerMode":"NA","supportsCsvDownloads":true,"cswRecords":[{"name":"Rb-Sr Isotope Data","resourceProvider":"Unknown","id":"af4e1d080246c13bd214b0289e922be2b8e38af9","recordInfoUrl":"https://portal.auscope.org.au/geonetwork/srv/eng/catalog.search#/metadata/af4e1d080246c13bd214b0289e922be2b8e38af9","description":"Analytical data tables for publicly-available Sr-isotope data from Geoscience Australia (GA). Each result links to information about the sample, analytical metadata, and the source publication. Refer to de Caritat et al. (2022a,b) for further details: https://dx.doi.org/10.26186/146397 and https://dx.doi.org/10.26186/147473.","noCache":false,"service":false,"adminArea":null,"contactOrg":"Geoscience Australia","contactPerson":null,"funderOrg":"Unknown","authors":[],"onlineResources":[{"url":"https://services.ga.gov.au/gis/geochronology-isotopes/wfs","type":"WFS","name":"isotope:isotopes_rbsr","description":"Rb-Sr Isotope Data","version":"","applicationPr